\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 BOD victims turn to \uc2 UN\uc2  human rights system for denial of justice\b0\par\par\uc2 2,864 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Legal representatives of 200 clients affected by the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and liquidation of four banks abroad owned by Grupo Financiero BOD, continue executing procedures in accordance with the provisions of the UN Human Rights Protection System. The group of people demanding the banker Victor Vargas to return their money is mostly made up of senior citizens from the states of Zulia, Aragua and Carabobo. Others died without having obtained a response to their claim from the TSJ and the Venezuelan State.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Leal died in 2020 due to problems associated with covid-19. At the time he became ill he did not have sufficient resources for adequate treatment and hospitalization. Since 2017 he lost all the money deposited in one of the four off shore banks of the BOD, owned by Victor Vargas, which were \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  and closed by the banking and financial authorities in 2020.\par \par \uc2 Precisely in 2017 he and his family realized for the first time that they could not transfer from one account to another, part of the deposits they had in Banco Orinoco NV in Cura\u231\'00\'E7ao, so a host of worries began. This uncertainty never calmed down given the answers of the bank employees that went from "they were changing from one correspondent bank to another" and that they should not worry "because the situation was going to be solved". But it never happened.\par \par \uc2 "We did not have money, at that time of Covid-19, we could hear that people with insurance or wealthy people could be hospitalized in a private clinic, but we had money in Banco Orinoco so that they could take care of him, we could never have access to it. We had to go to several clinics by ambulance and they would not receive him. Thank God we had the help of a doctor friend who offered to help us financially, but his health was already very delicate and in the 15 days he was hospitalized he could not survive", said a relative of Mr. Leal who asked not to be identified.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Leal's case is one of the 12,000 clients of \uc2 Banco Occidental de Descuento\uc2  (BOD) who are still waiting for the delivery of their money deposited in Banco Orinoco NV in Cura\u231\'00\'E7ao, BOI Bank in Antigua and Barbuda, All Bank Corp in Panama and Bancam\u233\'00\'E9rica (Banca M\u250\'00\'FAltiple de las Am\u233\'00\'E9ricas) in the Dominican Republic.\par \par \uc2 Many of those affected are individuals who opened accounts at the BOD headquarters in Venezuela, but part of their funds were sent to banks abroad belonging to the holding company Cartera de Inversiones Venezuela C.A., 99.57% owned by banker Victor Vargas Irausquin. The promise of higher returns for their investment in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in his banks outside the country was the argument to convince the clients; although others were neither consulted nor asked for authorization for the transfer of the funds.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Leal was a businessman of European descent and decided to distribute his inheritance during his lifetime to his children, who had the misfortune of making a decision whose consequence they never imagined: one of them decided to leave the money deposited in Banco Orinoco and the second in All Bank.\par \par \uc2 "We and a group of people decided in the first place to file a complaint with Sudeban with the help of Anauco and the lawyer Roberto Le\u243\'00\'F3n Parilli. Now today my family is facing problems, it is costing us a lot to keep what little we have left. I have friends who have helped me with the payment of my children's school fees and all this, without any need, since we have money to which we do not have access and which could solve many of our problems", said one of the members of the Leal family consulted by TalCual.\par \par \uc2 An unanswered case Lawyers Carlos Calder\u243\'00\'F3n and Roberto Hung, representing approximately 200 people, filed in October 2022 a lawsuit for collective and diffuse interests before the Constitutional Chamber of the Supreme Court of Justice (TSJ) against the BOD, as well as against its owner V\u237\'00\'EDctor Vargas and the holding company Cartera de Inversiones de Venezuela C.A.\par \par \uc2 The group of people demanding that the banker V\u237\'00\'EDctor Vargas return their money is mostly made up of senior citizens, customers from the states of Zulia, Aragua and Carabobo, in the capital city of Caracas, as well as retirees and former employees of the entity itself .\par \par \uc2 After this legal action, six months passed while waiting for a response from the Constitutional Chamber presided by Gladys Guti\u233\'00\'E9rrez, who is also the president of the TSJ. To date, only the administrative act has been admitted and it has not been decided whether to admit or reject the class action against the BOD. Due to the delay in the response of the highest court of the country within a maximum period of seven days, the case was referred to international courts.\par \par \uc2 At the beginning of May 2023, the lawyers went to the Office of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights (UNHCHR), Volker T\u252\'00\'FCrk (who was in Venezuela at the time), to denounce the Venezuelan State for denial of justice. They consider that there is a clear violation of fundamental rights such as access to justice and effective judicial protection.\par \par \uc2 "We have exhausted the legal channels in accordance with the regulations and the National Constitution. This situation reached its peak and this peak does not allow us to take a peaceful and legal path to resolve a conflict that involves a large number of people. The failure of the TSJ to make a pronouncement led us to go up a step and turn to the human rights protection system to which Venezuela is a party", stated Carlos Calder\u243\'00\'F3n.\par \par \uc2 By going to international human rights instances, the Venezuelan State is responsible, because it has caused a patrimonial damage and has not responded to this cause. The objective is also to take action for the protection of the user and the consumer.\par \par \uc2 "The articles of the Declaration of Human Rights of the United Nations Organization, which dates back to 1948 and refers to the right of every citizen to have access to justice in a neutral and independent court, are being violated; but the right to property is also being violated. In the face of all this, the Venezuelan legal system has not pronounced itself. There is absolute silence on the case, not even Victor Vargas has gone to court to deny the facts for which he is being sued," said Calderon.\par \par \uc2 Last Monday, June 26, a new document was sent to the Coordinator of the \uc2 Office of the UN High Commissioner for Human Rights\uc2  in Venezuela, to the members of the Working Group on the issue of human rights and transnational corporations and other business enterprises, to the Special Rapporteur on the independence of judges and lawyers and to the \uc2 UN\uc2  Special Rapporteur on the promotion of truth, justice, reparation and guarantees of non-repetition.\par \par \uc2 Lawyer Roberto Hung, specialist in Constitutional Procedural Law, explained that according to the special mechanisms of the Commission on Human Rights, the organization is empowered to send questionnaires to the judicial and financial authorities of Venezuela and of the other countries in which the subsidiary banks of the BOD operated.\par \par \uc2 The bodies mentioned in the document to which information is requested in Venezuela are the TSJ, Sudeban, the Attorney General's Office, the Autonomous Service of Registries and Notaries (Saren) and the National Bank of Credit; and abroad, the Superintendencies of Banks of Panama and the Dominican Republic, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Eastern Caribbean, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Curacao and Saint Marten. Likewise, to the Court of First Instance of Cura\u231\'00\'E7ao that heard the bankruptcy of Banco del Orinoco and to its liquidator and bankruptcy trustee Michiel Gorsira; as well as to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Uruguay\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Holland.\par \par \uc2 "In this additional brief that we submitted to the United Nations Human Rights Commission, we added new data related to the custodians of the assets of the subsidiary banks of the BOD, and we asked them to request information from these custodians as well. Three and a half years after what happened, it has not been possible to have access to the investment portfolio held by these custodians", highlighted Hung.\par \par \uc2 According to the information gathered for the lawsuit, it was learned that there are several custodians related to the BOD, one of them is Welden Securities de Uruguay Agente de Valores S.A., which in October 2020, that is, one year after the bankruptcy of the Venezuelan financial entity and two more years have passed to date, was sanctioned by the Superintendence of Financial Services of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Uruguay\uc2  for having incurred in irregularities regarding information safekeeping measures according to the regulations applicable in that nation.\par \par \uc2 After Welden Securities was terminated as a securities broker, it was authorized to withdraw the amounts deposited as collateral and to cancel the pledges and proceed with the corresponding returns.\par \par \uc2 Regarding the securities custodian agent Vistra International S.A. of Panama, the letter sent to the UN Human Rights Commission states that this company is not recognized as a Vistra International Investment firm, with global presence and \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 , "but corresponds to a regular trading company registered in Panama, of which it is not known if it is registered in any financial authority, for which verification tasks are being carried out".\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, Farringdon Asset Management, also mentioned as custodian of the securities of the BOD's subsidiary banks, is located in Singapore.\par \par \uc2 Calder\u243\'00\'F3n also indicated that in another of the actions carried out in this case, the lifting of the corporate veil of Cartera de Inversiones de Venezuela, owner of the BOD and its banks abroad, was requested. This figure would allow the company or its shareholders to respond with their patrimony.\par \par \uc2 "We have been unprotected". On September 19, 2020, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the banks located in the Caribbean occurred and four days later in \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the Superintendence of Banks and Other Financial Institutions (Sudeban) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  the BOD because the patrimony of the Venezuelan entity was affected. Seven days later, another administrative action of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took place for violating anti-money laundering regulations, which lasted two and a half years. This process was then lifted to give way to the sale of the entity owned by Victor Vargas to the Banco Nacional de Cr\u233\'00\'E9dito (BNC).\par \par \uc2 All this was happening before the eyes of those affected by the BOD, who had the hope that with the negotiation with the BNC, there would be a resolution in their favor, which was nothing more than the return of their lost or withheld deposits. Several of them -by the way- stated that their problems with this bank are of long standing.\par \par \uc2 Giuseppe Tirrito, whose Italian family arrived in Venezuela and settled in Zulia State, pointed out that his parents opened an account in Banco Maracaibo, which years later was bought and merged by Victor Vargas' BOD. At the same time they kept part of their deposits in the US bank International Bank located in Miami (United States), which belonged to the Venezuelan group. In 1999 they found out that their deposits had been transferred to BOI Bank without having been consulted.\par \par \uc2 "The only arguments they gave when we demanded an answer as to why they were moving the money without having asked for authorization was that BOI Bank was a better bank and that they were going to give us a better return. They tricked my mother by telling her that they were going to give her a debit card, checkbooks and they never gave her anything", he said.\par \par \uc2 Tirrito pointed out that despite the fact that they have gone to Venezuelan governmental entities to solve the case, "because they are the ones who protect the citizen and it turns out that this has not been the case, because only Victor Vargas and the BOD have been protected. We have denounced before Sudeban, before the Attorney General's Office. We have been left unprotected".\par \par \uc2 Approximately 50 people in Maracaibo have adhered to the lawsuit filed before the TSJ. "We never traveled abroad to open an account in this bank, none of those affected by the BOD personally opened an account in the countries where these banks were located", said Tirrito.\par \par \uc2 In the lawsuit filed before the TSJ, it is stated that it has been known that the BOD has delivered part of the deposits to several of its clients, by negotiating with them a payment in money and/or property, but many of them are companies or legal entities.\par \par \uc2 William, is another of those affected who lives in the city of Maracay in Aragua State and works as a merchant. He told that after years of being clients of the BOD and when in 2014 they were offered to deposit their money in Banco Orinoco, they never imagined finding themselves in a situation of this type.\par \par \uc2 "We had a good relationship with the bank and with the bank's managers. In 2017 everything started to go wrong, because when we needed the money we could not access the resources. They told us that they were going to help us and it was all a lie, so in 2019 we sent a communication to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Cura\u231\'00\'E7ao and they never gave us an answer," said William, who is a representative of the Asian Community of Maracay-Valencia.\par \par \uc2 He pointed out that at that time, he and a group of 10 people also in the same situation decided to meet and evaluate the steps to follow. "Several of my countrymen are in this situation.Three of us went to Cura\u231\'00\'E7ao to the bank and what they told us was that why \u168\'00\'A8jurungar' (review) this issue and, that we had to wait".\par \par \uc2 The cases of those affected by the BOD have different stories. William commented that one of his acquaintances decided to withdraw his money that he had in a bank in Germany to deposit it in one of Vargas Irausqu\u237\'00\'EDn's entities and, "he was never able to recover it and that person died. What we see is a lot of liveliness, they are using our money and we don't know where they took it. This is unethical. We want justice. It is a bank that can make its investments, but they should protect their clients' money".\par \par \uc2 For the lawyer Roberto Hung "we are facing an important case in financial matters, of \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  initiated in Venezuela. It is already something systematic, it is not just one person or a group of 100 affected".\par \par \uc2 He recalled that Venezuela does not currently have a large banking sector, but it is very striking that an entity such as the BOD, located in the stratum of large banks in the country, has carried out actions that affected a large number of customers and that no responsibilities have been established.\par \par \uc2 Among those affected are also former employees and retirees of the BOD who had a collective contract with insurance plans; as well as shareholders or minority partners.\par \par \uc2 "As an employee of the bank through an incentive plan that had been developed in the financial institution, we received those incentives in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . When I left the BOD I was left with practically all of the money held back since 2017, without being able to have any kind of access or from the web page, while the cards were suspended," recounted a former employee of the Venezuelan bank who asked not to be identified.\par \par \uc2 In his opinion, the case already borders on the affectation of human rights, since he was diagnosed with an illness that kept him in a delicate situation and he could not count on his savings to pay for his treatment.\par \par \uc2 "It was a very complicated situation and, I lived and knew of other stories of families affected by this case, many also sick with cancer, others who lost their homes and vehicles, merchants who lost lines of credit they had outside the country, foundations that were also customers, in short, various situations. This has been a complex story and unfortunately no one from the bank has shown their face and whether the money exists or not. There is absolute silence".\par \par \uc2 The former BOD worker stressed that the "issue became a mystery and there is no possibility of calling anyone to ask for information", after the sale of the entity to the BNC, which, by the way, was left with only the assets and "healthy liabilities", that is to say, without the portfolio of the banks abroad. "How did a case of this magnitude come to be in this situation? We are talking about some $1.2 billion. Although the banks where those resources were located were in banks abroad, the holding company or owner is the BOD. All these affected clients are Venezuelan and they arrived there because they were clients of the BOD. It has already been a long time, everything is in limbo, it is as if those banks had never existed".\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230703ej730078i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
