\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Will the \uc2 BCV\uc2  be able to contain the dollar increase? This is what two economists explain\b0\par\par\uc2 1,210 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Mai 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The quotations of the official and parallel dollar once again show an upward trend, passing the 26 and 28 bolivars barrier, respectively.\par \par \uc2 In the last months -April and May-, the exchange rate had remained stable, due to the banking \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 BCV\uc2 ), through the use of international reserves. A policy that has been criticized by economists on several occasions.\par \par \uc2 Economists Tamara Herrera and Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Guerra asserted that, despite the efforts of the national Executive to contain the price of the dollar, it is "inevitable" that the trend will continue to rise.\par \par \uc2 "The national Executive is trying to use less foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and that is why the emphasis is rather on containing (public) spending, administering at its discretion the increases in bonuses and labor bonuses", said Herrera, chief economist of S\u237\'00\'EDntesis Financiera.\par \par \uc2 This would even be the reason why Maduro did not increase the minimum wage on May 1st. "It is so as not to have turbulent episodes, out of control in July and at the end of the year", he added.\par \par \uc2 For the economist, "the rise of the dollar is inevitable". However, he considers that what the government is trying to do is to keep the exchange rate "under control, because it is the only way it has to decelerate inflation".\par \par \uc2 In addition, "the government is using other restrictive instruments to avoid a rise in the exchange rate and to use less foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but little by little, in spite of the economic slowdown, there are signs of a certain revival in the demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . It may be because of some economic activity or because of some expectation of concern in the market", pointed out Herrera.\par \par \uc2 Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of almost $95 million In this sense, the economist and member of the Venezuelan Finance Observatory (OVF), Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Guerra pointed out that last Monday the \uc2 BCV\uc2  made a bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of almost $95 million, with the purpose of keeping the exchange rate stable.\par \par \uc2 This would be "the highest figure so far this year in one day and that says a lot about their intention to contain the rise of the dollar", but "my thesis has always been that it is not possible to sustain the stability of the exchange rate for a long time for a very simple reason: the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  does not have the dollars to do so", argued Guerra.\par \par \uc2 He pointed out that the \uc2 BCV\uc2  has resorted to a "mixture of very strong policies", which is based on containing public expenditure and bank reserve requirements, which "prevents the effect of bank credit and obviously the increase of monetary liquidity, but I do not see that it is possible to sustain (the dollar) for a long time and I have been warning about it", he added.\par \par \uc2 Guerra warned that the instability in the exchange rate will have an effect on inflation in the coming months.\par \par \uc2 "To stabilize the exchange rate we need resources, dollars, because this is not a problem of bolivars but of dollars. And if it had not been for \uc2 Chevron\uc2  and the dollars it is selling, the exchange rate would be close to 40 bolivars per dollar, I calculate, it is difficult to know the level, but clearly it would have depreciated much more", he affirmed.\par \par \uc2 The economist emphasized that the Executive "is having cash flow problems, despite the fact that it is exporting more barrels of oil. The price of oil has decreased and this reduces its cash flow. They do not have an economic stabilization fund, they did not save in the time of abundance and now they do not have enough foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ".\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BCV\uc2  will continue "squeezing" the international reserves. Both economists agreed that the \uc2 BCV\uc2  will continue to squeeze international reserves to curb the rise of the dollar.\par \par \uc2 "Given how restrictive (the government) is being in fiscal matters -I am referring to spending and taxes- it is looking to spend less foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , allocate less international reserves to that. In fact, we think that 2.8 billion dollars would be enough for the year, which is less than the 3.7 billion dollars allocated last year" in banking \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , said Herrera.\par \par \uc2 He clarified that one thing is the amount of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  allocated by the \uc2 BCV\uc2  to the national banks and another what the banks manage to sell.\par \par \uc2 "There has been a lot of bank liquidity and that has required less injection of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the strong bank injection made last February, which in a single week was 280 million dollars. After that they dried up the market and with that there are less foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  requirements", asserted Herrera.\par \par \uc2 According to S\u237\'00\'EDntesis Financiera's estimates, so far in 2023, net sales of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  amount to approximately US$ 610 million.\par \par \uc2 "According to our calculation that US$ 2,800 million would be required, there would still be US$ 2,000 million to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , unless they can become much more severe and recessive in fiscal matters", the economist pointed out.\par \par \uc2 For his part, Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Guerra affirmed that the Maduro administration has two ways to control the \uc2 BCV\uc2  exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 "One, they use the international reserves, which is what they have been doing. And two, the dollars that are in Venezuela and the international credit cards, which fall in an account of each bank and then go to the \uc2 BCV\uc2  on Mondays to be sold", he explained.\par \par \uc2 However, in his opinion, none of this is enough if Venezuelans do not recover their confidence in the bolivar, since they continue "repudiating" the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as a result of the economic instability, inflation, devaluation and depreciation.\par \par \uc2 "Dollar they put in the market, dollar the market swallows", expressed Guerra, who calculated that at least 160 million dollars have been destined to bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far in May.\par \par \uc2 How much would the dollar close at in May? Regarding the projections of the amount at which the exchange rate of the official and parallel dollar could close by the end of May, Herrera does not believe that it will reach 30 bolivars per dollar.\par \par \uc2 "We see that rate at the end of June, assuming that there is a certain normality in the rate of exchange \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Even, depending on how successful this maintenance of such strong bank illiquidity may be, June may pass without passing that barrier (of 30 bolivars per dollar)", he warned.\par \par \uc2 He explained that the above scenario is in the event that no event occurs that generates "uncertainty or nervousness" in the current economic scenario of the country. Otherwise, "demand will be exacerbated and the price will get out of control", added Tamara Herrera.\par \par \uc2 Guerra preferred to reserve his estimates, but made it clear that for the rest of the year the trend will be that the depreciation of the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue.\par \par \uc2 "I do not dare to say it, I do not have elements and I do not believe that anyone has them to accurately project, but the trend clearly is the depreciation of the bolivar for the remainder of the year. There is no doubt about that", stated the OVF member.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230528ej5s008tb\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
