\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Economist Luis Oliveros forecasts "couple of months of low inflation".\b0\par\par\uc2 450 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 April 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 In the last few weeks, the official exchange rate seems to have stagnated around 24 bolivars per dollar, after the \uc2 BCV\b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market for about $180 million in a single day, last February 13. The stability of the dollar has reduced inflation, as the prices of goods and services tied to foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  do not increase as frequently.\par \par \uc2 Venezuelans could have a break from the incessant increase in prices that has plagued the economy in the last months, since in March there was a deceleration in the monthly variation of inflation, according to studies of the Venezuelan Observatory of Finance (OVF).\par \par \uc2 With an inflation variation of only 4% for March, economist Luis Oliveros considers that Venezuela could expect a couple of months of low inflation, depending on the context and the incentives that the exchange market may have.\par \par \uc2 The key, for Oliveros, is for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 BCV\uc2 ) to maintain its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy to keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market under control, although he warns that it will depend on the amount of money they can inject.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation in March, according to the Venezuelan Finance Observatory, was a little over 4%, something expected due to, among other things, the minimal variation of the exchange rate. It seems that we have a couple of months of low inflation ahead of us. The key will be whether the \uc2 BCV\uc2  has enough foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to inject into the market", he argued.\par \par \uc2 In the last few weeks the official exchange rate seems to have stagnated at around 24 bolivars per dollar, after months of spontaneous price increases that caused chaos in the national commerce and destroyed the already very low minimum wages in force in the country for the last year.\par \par \uc2 The stability of the exchange rate has caused the prices of goods and services anchored to the dollar to maintain a certain stability, although the national economy has experienced price increases even in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 By the time the price of the dollar began to stagnate, in mid-February, it was reported that the \uc2 BCV\uc2  applied the largest sale of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market it has made so far, with .\par \par \uc2 However, with the scarce foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  available to the Government, it seems difficult for them to maintain the constant injection of dollars to the exchange market.\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, experts have warned that this is a superficial measure, since when the tap of dollars ends, the demand for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market will be much higher than the supply, which will cause an abrupt increase in the price of the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230410ej49000jl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
