\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 BCV\uc2  narrows the gap between the official dollar and the parallel dollar through bank  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2  exceeding $540 million\b0\par\par\uc2 875 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Februar 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 BCV\uc2 ) carried out last Monday, February 13, the largest \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  so far in 2023, with a sale of 180 million dollars to the banking system, according to the calculations of the firm S\u237\'00\'EDntesis Financiera. A measure that continues reducing the gap in the exchange rate of the official dollar compared to the parallel dollar.\par \par \uc2 According to figures from the consulting firm, last week it was reduced to 1.7% versus 3.9% of the previous week. In part, this is due to the strong exchange \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  carried out by the issuing entity.\par \par \uc2 "It was a product of the more intense acceleration in the official exchange rate. For the fifth consecutive week, the difference between both markers (BCV vs Parallel Rate) has been reduced", the firm detailed in its \uc2 Twitter\uc2  account. In this sense, how much has the \uc2 BCV\uc2  injected to the market so far in February, and is the government able to continue sustaining this rhythm? And, what can be foreseen, at least, in the first quarter of 2023?\par \par \uc2 Tamara Herrera, economist and head of S\u237\'00\'EDntesis Financiera, commented that with the last exchange \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  made by the \uc2 BCV\uc2 , it surpassed the allocation it made in the whole of 2022.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 BCV\uc2  had been injecting a slightly lower amount than last year, but on Monday 13 (February) it suddenly tripled the allocation and with that it reaches 540 million dollars and exceeds the allocation of 2022 (460 million dollars)", she said.\par \par \uc2 The economist assured that with this increase the \uc2 BCV\uc2  sought three effects: "a) To quickly dry up the bank surpluses available for credit; b) To take advantage of the Carnival week, usually of very low exchange activity and 3) To change the negative expectations by giving some sign of financial strength".\par \par \uc2 In his opinion, "it is most likely that, given the relative scarcity of bolivars in the economy, the public will not have the capacity to absorb this allocation in the same week".\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, Herrera reminded that Venezuela is in its usual "tax payment cycle, which generates that relative shortage of bolivars to pay the annual tax liquidation that concludes on March 31. After that date, it will be seen if oil revenues improve enough, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \uc2 PDVSA\uc2 , to keep the exchange rate moderately contained for the rest of the year".\par \par \uc2 Economist Herrera warned that "the challenge is not small, because the Asian market is very competitive and because the clean-up of the gigantic corruption that has taken place in \uc2 PDVSA\uc2  under the protection of the sanctions will be short-lived if there is no transparency and accountability in the industry".\par \par \uc2 BCV\uc2  surpassed US$ 150 million in February The economist and member of the Venezuelan Finance Observatory (OVF), Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Guerra, ratified that "Monday 13 was the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  record", but so far in February the issuing entity surpassed 150 million dollars in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 "This with the purpose of mitigating and moderating the depreciation trend that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  itself has imposed on the dollar, with the objective of bringing it closer to the parallel", he added.\par \par \uc2 However, the economist highlighted that so far in 2023, "the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Venezuela\uc2  has lost 273 million dollars of its international reserves. It is the biggest loss in a month and a half in a long time, in fact, last year in the first two months the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not lose a single dollar of its reserves, simply because it did not make important \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 ", he pointed out.\par \par \uc2 When asked about the capacity of Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro's administration to continue sustaining the rhythm of exchange \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and, therefore, maintain the price of the dollar, Guerra was clear: "It is very difficult".\par \par \uc2 For the economist, "this will basically depend on two things: 1) On the entry of dollars that will have improved and increased due to the exports being made by \uc2 Chevron\uc2 , which is already exporting more than 50,000 barrels per day, half of which are being collected, and 2) Most Venezuelans do not want bolivars, so the dollars that enter the market, dollars that disappear, because all those who have bolivars go out to buy dollars, precisely because of the inflation that is accelerating", he said.\par \par \uc2 In this sense, he insisted that it is very difficult for the \uc2 BCV\uc2  to continue sustaining the rhythm of bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "To lose 270 million dollars in a month and a half is to lose almost 2 billion dollars in the year, a very substantial figure for Venezuela. So, I don't see it as possible", he pointed out.\par \par \uc2 Furthermore, he considers that if the Government accelerates spending in bolivars, "those bolivars go against the dollar, so it is not easy to stabilize the exchange rate at this time".\par \par \uc2 For the first quarter of 2023, Guerra calculates that "there will be no stabilization of the exchange rate as long as there is not an abundant supply of dollars", so inflation expectations are very high.\par \par \uc2 "The enemy of exchange rate stability is not having reserves, that people do not want bolivars, and precisely the high inflation", concluded the economist.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230220ej2k008rp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
