\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 BCV\uc2  sold a record $180 million to banks this #13Feb.\b0\par\par\uc2 512 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Februar 2023\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 So far this year 2023, the amount of the \uc2 BCV\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  has already reached US$ 569 million, i.e., US$ 68 million above the amount sold as of the same date in 2022\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 BCV\uc2 ) carried out the largest \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with a sale of US$ 180 million to the banks' \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  desks on Monday, February 13. The purpose is to increase the supply of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in view of a possible greater injection of liquidity in bolivars to the market, due, among other factors, to the increase in bonds paid through the Sistema Patria.\par \par \uc2 So far this year, the price of \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  rose 8.46% in a total of 15 foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  placements in the banking system, including \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  and their extensions, reported the portal Banca y Negocios.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 BCV\uc2  has been making more frequent sales, with the objective of maintaining an adequate level of supply to counteract, by that means, an even greater depreciation of the bolivar", the news portal pointed out.\par \par \uc2 So far in February, the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 269 million dollars to banks, which allows projecting an important increase compared to the approximately 300 million dollars it placed in January.\par \par \uc2 In fact, with the record sale of this February 13, the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  expenditure already reaches 569 million dollars in 2023, 68 million above the figure sold on the same date in 2022.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy seems to be achieving a core objective of the exchange rate plan, which is to keep the official exchange rate competitive, since the gap in favor of the parallel exchange rate was, at the opening of this Monday, February 13, at a meager 2.36%.\par \par \uc2 The issuing entity increased in 21% the number of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sale \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to banks, but increased in 252% the amount of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2022, closing at $5,400 million, an average of $450 million per month, and which reflected a variation of 251.7% compared to the $1,535 million it sold to banks in 2021.\par \par \uc2 This \uc2 BCV\uc2  policy is executed at the expense of its low international reserves and thanks to a timid increase in oil revenues and a significant variation in the price of a barrel of Venezuelan crude oil. According to official figures, the agency's resources ended 2022 at $9,946 million, i.e., below the $10,937 million of the beginning of the year.\par \par \uc2 According to calculations of local consultants, a good part of the foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  resources offered in the official market come directly from the cash of \uc2 Petr\u243\'00\'F3leos de \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  (PDVSA)\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BCV\uc2  made 52 \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2022, but if extensions are counted, the number of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales to banks rises to 82, the highest annual volume since this policy was implemented in May 2019. Despite the \uc2 BCV\uc2 's strong \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the bolivar depreciated 74% against the dollar in 2022, being considered one of the periods of the highest devaluation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020230214ej2e00bsj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
