ts usual load of political interpretations to an economic phenomenon, has awakened fears of a return to rigid controls or the deepening of deterrents to the holding of dollars".\par \par \uc2 Therefore, he concludes that "the only effective way to contain the depreciation of the bolivar is to strengthen the demand for money. The reluctance to hold bolivars is what persistently leads to seek refuge in solid assets, either inventories or dollars, which is almost the same thing given the high imported component of the goods that serve as refuge".\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020221214eice00byl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
