\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Unchecked inflation: Venezuelan  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  devaluates 17% against the dollar in less than a week\b0\par\par\uc2 608 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Dezember 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The Venezuelan bolivar recorded a 17% devaluation against the dollar in the last week, whose price has increased rapidly both in the official and parallel markets, where it surpassed 14 and 18 bolivars, respectively, this Friday.\par \par \uc2 In seven days, the price of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the official market increased 20 %, rising from 11.69 bolivars to 14.12 bolivars, according to the reports of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 BCV\uc2 ), which reports daily the average quotation resulting from the \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the exchange desks of the banking institutions.\par \par \uc2 In the parallel market, on the other hand, the increase in the price of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , used in most commercial transactions in the country, has been greater, soaring from 13.78 bolivars to 18.26 bolivars, an increase of 32% in one week, according to the Monitor D\u243\'00\'F3lar Venezuela portal, which offers the daily quotation taking into account several markers.\par \par \uc2 Thus, the bolivar devalued 24% against the dollar quoted in the unofficial market.\par \par \uc2 Wages and pensions\par \par \uc2 The minimum wage and pensions, fixed at 130 bolivars last March, have since lost 69% of their value, as a result of the devaluation of the bolivar.\par \par \uc2 These incomes, at the official exchange rate, went from US$ 29.68 to US$ 9.20, thus sinking the salary and pensions even further, below the extreme poverty threshold per income range established by the \uc2 World Bank\uc2 , of US$ 1.90 per day, at US$ 0.30 per day.\par \par \uc2 Venezuelan economist and associate professor at \uc2 IE University\uc2  in Madrid Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Manuel Puente told EFE that the Caribbean country's impoverishment "has been overwhelming, a consequence of the government's very poor economic policy management," even in the midst of rising oil prices.\par \par \uc2 "Venezuela is in the midst of an oil boom, a consequence of the Russia-Ukraine war, in which Venezuelan oil prices, which reached 92 dollars, today are in the order of 70 dollars, but it is still an extraordinary price for Venezuela to be experiencing these terrible exchange imbalances with terrible impacts on wages", he explained.\par \par \uc2 The strategy\par \par \uc2 The Madurist dictatorship has been applying a strategy to contain the exchange rate which consists of controlling the demand for dollars, reducing the issuance of bolivars -necessary to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 - through the reduction of public expenditure and the restriction of financing.\par \par \uc2 However, in the last months, the Venezuelan regime increased spending with several payments to public workers, at the same time that it has been releasing credits, which increased 123 % in the last year.\par \par \uc2 For his part, economist and university professor Ronald Balza Guanipa told EFE that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has increased "the issuance of bolivars for government spending" in "activities it is carrying out at the moment" that are unknown, in addition to the payment of Christmas bonuses to public sector employees.\par \par \uc2 At the same time, he pointed out that the \uc2 BCV\uc2  has also reduced the sale of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  with which it had been feeding the supply to contain the exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 However, according to Balza Guanipa, it is difficult to know what the supply of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is due to the fact that it is not known how many dollars are circulating or how many are entering the nation from the sale of oil and other exports due to the lack of official data.\par \par \uc2 (With information from EFE)\par \par \uc2 Bolivar devaluated almost 7 % against the dollar in one day\par \par \uc2 Price controls in \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  denounced as an "artificial \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 " by Chavism\par \par \uc2 Chavista justice sentenced to 30 years in prison to a married couple who had been acquitted\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020221210eica004h5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
