\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 BCV\uc2  significantly lowered foreign  \highlight22\uc2 currency \highlight\uc2  sales to protect international reserves\b0\par\par\uc2 945 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 August 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BCV\uc2  slowed down its rate of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales to banking exchange desks in order to safeguard the already depleted international reserves. In spite of the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the price of the dollar continues to rise and remains at the new ceiling of 6 bolivars.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 BCV\uc2 ) continues to have limitations. Despite the increase in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  inflows to the country, due to the rebound in oil prices, the international reserves are not enough to keep the exchange rate at bay.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BCV\uc2  considerably reduced its sale of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the banks' \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  desks, going from 100 million dollars per week to 60 million dollars, but it also divided the delivery of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in two parts.\par \par \uc2 The consultant's data indicates that on Monday, August 1st, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allocated a little more than $45 million and on Wednesday, August 3rd, it complemented with $15 million, achieving small reversals in the exchange rate in those two days of 0.3% and 0.1%, respectively.\par \par \uc2 In spite of the fact that the price of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had a lower growth rate since last year, due to the monetary policy implemented by the issuing entity to restrict liquidity, its quotation in the exchange system reached the 6 bolivars ceiling. While the \uc2 BCV\uc2 's exchange rate has not reached this ceiling, it always follows in its footsteps.\par \par \uc2 Since January 29, 2019, the \uc2 BCV\uc2  started its exchange \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  plan with the purpose of "achieving stability in exchange and monetary matters and stopping hyperinflation".\par \par \uc2 The measure is based on the fact that the agency injects foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and withdraws the necessary bolivars to the banking entities, in order to maintain the defined exchange rate target. Since the beginning of the exchange \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , it was decided that they would be weekly,\par \par \uc2 Economist Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Guerra recently recalled that the inconsistency of the economic policy based on a fiscal expansion and an expansion of inorganic money by the issuing entity, in a context of exchange control with a fixed preferential rate since 2007, was depleting the international reserves and giving way to the economic collapse of the country.\par \par \uc2 In addition to this, he warned that the \uc2 BCV\uc2  has "excessively burned reserves" in a clearly wrong policy to contain devaluation and inflation.\par \par \uc2 "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  perceives that this inflation is a transitory phenomenon, that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is depreciating due to a circumstantial factor, the correct thing to do is to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  and sell foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stabilize this inflation. But if the trend is permanent, because the exchange rate is depreciating due to the fact that people do not want the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the right thing to do is not to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  because, if you \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 , you start to deplete the reserves," Guerra said .\par \par \uc2 Tamara Herrera, director of S\u237\'00\'EDntesis Financiera, explained that central banks have instruments to control the monetary mass and in the case of Venezuela, the availability of bolivars in the money market; but they do not have instruments in dollars because they do not issue in that foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . "The difference is in how they do it", he said.\par \par \uc2 With this statement he hints that if positive results are not obtained in the execution of the monetary and exchange policy, people will continue to look for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the protection of their resources.\par \par \uc2 "Everyone, whether a company or an individual, every time they have a surplus in bolivars, they continue to look for hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the reason is merely transactional, because the propensity and the need for imports continues to increase. Also for hedging purposes, until it is not convinced or the very slow stabilization that is being sought is not achieved", stated Herrera.\par \par \uc2 Guerra reiterated that for any nation, not having sufficient reserves "is a very serious problem", since it cannot meet its foreign debt commitments and for the payment of imports.\par \par \uc2 "Why is it that even though the price of oil is at an all-time high, the \uc2 BCV\uc2 , instead of gaining and accumulating international reserves, is losing them? Something does not add up, where are the reals, asked the economist.\par \par \uc2 According to figures from the consulting firm Ecoanal\u237\'00\'EDtica, the administration of Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro has 154% more income in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the year 2022. In addition to an inter-annual increase of 104.5% of the equivalent tax collection in dollars.\par \par \uc2 In its report, S\u237\'00\'EDntesis Financiera pointed out that the agency did not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market when the increases were more intense: 0.9% and 0.4% on Thursday, August 4 and Friday, August 5.\par \par \uc2 "In short, it tolerated an acceleration of the rate of depreciation to 1.3% in the week, compared to 1.1% in the previous week and 0.6% in the week before that," the consulting firm pointed out.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 BCV\uc2 's international reserves have remained at around US$10 billion. According to the last figure shown in its web page of August 8, they closed at $10.3 billion. This amount means a drop of $620 million with respect to the beginning of 2022 and of $981 million compared to the $11,281 million of a year ago.\par \par \uc2 S\u237\'00\'EDntesis Financiera considers -however- that the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase in the next days, but at most to $80 million and could repeat the behavior of the previous week, splitting the sale of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in two portions.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 BCV\uc2  doses its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to save reserves for weeks of greater monetary pressure", explained the consultant in the report.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220810ei8a00912\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
