\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Monthly inflation accelerates again to 10.1% in May\b0\par\par\uc2 890 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 7 Juni 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Economist Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Guerra stresses that the economic policy employed by Chavismo must change, since not even with all the reforms implemented is inflation being effectively contained.\par \par \uc2 The shadow of inflation looms over the Venezuelan economy months after believing to have controlled it, since for the second time this year a double digit figure is registered, after surpassing a 2021 with single digit percentages.\par \par \uc2 According to the figures of the Venezuelan Finance Observatory (OVF), inflation during the month of May stood at 10.1%, almost tripling the 3.6% recorded during April.\par \par \uc2 This increase is reminiscent of the 10.5% that the OVF reported in April, which now does not seem to be indicative of an isolated case but of a pattern of accelerating inflation, despite the fact that it is far from reaching the levels of hyperinflation that the country suffered between 2018 and 2020.\par \par \uc2 The economist and founder of the OVF, Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Guerra, warned that this is a considerably high figure compared to the monthly records evidenced in 2021, since with it Venezuela maintains the path towards a three-digit annual inflation.\par \par \uc2 "Inflation is not totally defeated as we had assumed. We are back to double digits, which is a considerably high figure. We had been in single digits for several times. Now there is an inflationary rebound," he highlighted in the presentation of the monthly inflationary report via Zoom.\par \par \uc2 With this update, cumulative inflation from January to May is already 34.4%. In addition, the year-on-year variation from May 2021 to May 2022 stands at 151%, still a three-digit figure.\par \par \uc2 "Although we are not at hyperinflation levels, one of 10% per month still marks a triple-digit inflationary course. Although it is evidently lower than those we have seen in hyperinflation processes, it is still worrying", insisted Guerra.\par \par \uc2 The report also highlights the list of items with the highest increases during the month. This month presented the particularity of presenting a considerable price increase in the education sector, due to the adjustment of tuition fees for the next academic year. The list of increases presents the following items:\par \par \uc2 Education: 54.9%. Miscellaneous goods and services: 24.8%. Recreation: 16%. Clothing and footwear: 18.6%. Housing rentals: 13.2% Food: 11.9% Housingrentals: 13.2% Housingrentals: 13.2% Housingrentals: 13.2% Housingrentals: 13.2% Housingrentals Food: 11.9%Food: 11.9% Transportation Transport: 11.5%Transportation: 11.5% Causes behind the accelerated inflation Causes behind the accelerated inflation For Guerra, there are multiple reasons that explain this acceleration of inflation and much has to do with the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 BCV\uc2 ) in the exchange market, as it failed to control the dollar exchange rate.\par \par \uc2 "The \uc2 BCV\uc2  was unable to stabilize the exchange rate during the month that concluded. In fact, the exchange rate increased 14.8%. That increase is passed on to the prices of goods, not only tradable goods, but also non-tradable goods such as services or student fees because the dollar is used as a reference for the price increase", he reasoned.\par \par \uc2 The issuing entity used $158 million to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the exchange market in April, one of the highest amounts it has injected from the international reserves, which continue to deteriorate due to this policy.\par \par \uc2 Guerra warns that if such huge injections continue throughout the year, the international reserves will be emptied. For this same reason, the OVF notes that in June the trend has not been the same and the \uc2 BCV\uc2  is injecting fewer dollars.\par \par \uc2 Another crucial aspect is international inflation. Thanks to the international trade crisis unleashed by the covid-19 pandemic and now Russia's conflict with Ukraine, inflation soared globally. Goods imported into Venezuela have a higher price and this is also reflected in the inflation figures.\par \par \uc2 Regardless of the reasons, Guerra stresses that the economic policy employed by Chavismo must change, since not even with all the reforms implemented is inflation being effectively contained.\par \par \uc2 "An economy blocked by credit, with strong \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and still the inflation rate is 10%. That means that something is not working," he stressed.\par \par \uc2 Food did not increase too much The family food basket measured by the OVF barely increased $1, going from $381 in April to $382 in May. Although the increase was tiny, it still remains the highest price it has been since the observatory has been measuring the prices of basic food goods.\par \par \uc2 This figure means that the majority of the country cannot have access to a food basket that satisfies the basic food needs of a Venezuelan family, since the minimum wages averaged in the private sector barely support a third of the basket, while the minimum wage of the public administration can only buy 10% of the products.\par \par \uc2 Those most affected by this disparity between salaries and the price of goods are pensioners. The elderly population is a victim of the inequality gaps that are becoming more and more accentuated in the new Venezuelan economy.\par \par \uc2 "They are leaving out of the scope of consumption important sectors of the Venezuelan population with an income of $30 of the minimum wage. We are talking about 3.2 million pensioners and close to 700,000 employees of the public administration", says Guerra.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220607ei6700af7\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
