\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Opposition congressman demanded quarterly adjustment for Venezuelan pensioners\b0\par\par\uc2 456 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2022\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The opposition deputy of the Parliament of Venezuela Jos\u233\'00\'E9 Gregorio Correa requested Monday to the regime of Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro to increase and adjust quarterly pensions collected by retired public workers, in proportion to inflation.\par \par \uc2 "Pensions should be adjusted and increased quarterly, according to inflation figures for a better living of our young (seniors) third and fourth age," said the parliamentarian in a press release.\par \par \uc2 Correa recalled that these are people "who gave their best years and do not receive adequate remuneration" and who deserve to age "with dignity and respect".\par \par \uc2 He assured that, from the Parliament, he will work so that pensioners and retirees "have the claims they deserve".\par \par \uc2 In recent days, the deputy asked his colleagues in the National Assembly (NA, Parliament) to think of this group as one of the priorities for the legislative agenda of the year that has just begun.\par \par \uc2 "We have to have a new year where retirees are also a priority (...) and that the State has the obligation to take care of each one of those Venezuelans who served to make, for many years, the public administration what it is," said the deputy on that occasion.\par \par \uc2 Correa also asked that the budget approved for 2022, which amounts to more than 13.457 billion dollars, include improvements for the country's retirees, including a benefit that allows them to "live with dignity".\par \par \uc2 Last month, the Venezuelan Observatory of Finance (OVF) indicated that monthly inflation in Venezuela was 6% in November, year-on-year inflation stood at 769%, and cumulative inflation was 616.9%.\par \par \uc2 "The items with the highest increases during the month in reference were health with 18.6%, goods and services with 16.5%, food 11.5% and footwear 9.8%," the organization said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The OVF said that, as in previous months, the behavior of prices responds to the "stability" that has maintained the exchange rate in the Caribbean country, where "recorded an increase of 5.7%, in line with the rise in prices," a percentage much lower than usual, linking months with double digits.\par \par \uc2 However, the observatory said that this policy of stability resulted in the fall of international reserves.\par \par \uc2 "This policy of exchange rate stability was expressed in a drop of US$171 million in the liquid international reserves of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 BCV\uc2 ), as a result of sustained \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by offering dollars in cash," the NGO explained.\par \par \uc2 (With information from EFE)\par \par \uc2 CONTINUE READING:\par \par \uc2 The opposition National Assembly ratified \uc2 Juan Guaid\u243\'00\'F3\uc2  as president in charge of Venezuela and of the Parliament\par \par \uc2 Venezuelan opposition criticized dictator Nicolas Maduro for conditioning dialogue in Mexico\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020220104ei14009xs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
