\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The Venezuelan Observatory of Finance reported cumulative inflation of 616% through November\b0\par\par\uc2 391 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Dezember 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Monthly inflation in Venezuela was 6 % last November, reported Tuesday the Venezuelan Observatory of Finance (OVF), an independent entity that brings together several economic analysts, who detailed that the year-on-year stood at 769 %, and at 616.9 % the accumulated one.\par \par \uc2 "The items with the highest increases during the month in reference were health with 18.6%, goods and miscellaneous services with 16.5%, food 11.5% and footwear 9.8%," the organization said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 The OVF said that, as in previous months, the behavior of prices responds to the "stability" that has maintained the exchange rate in the Caribbean country, where "recorded an increase of 5.7%, in line with the rise in prices," a percentage much lower than usual, to link months with double digits.\par \par \uc2 However, the observatory said that this policy of stability resulted in the fall of international reserves.\par \par \uc2 "This policy of exchange rate stability was expressed in a drop of 171 million dollars in the liquid international reserves of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 BCV\uc2 ), as a result of the sustained \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the issuing institution in the exchange market by offering dollars in cash," the NGO explained.\par \par \uc2 The organization explained that this stabilization in the exchange rate also contributed to the slower pace of expansion of the regime's spending, which resulted in a 5% increase in the monetary base during November, and generated that the prices of goods produced in Venezuela are "relatively expensive, compared to imported goods".\par \par \uc2 "When comparing the annualized inflation rate observed in November 2021 of 769 %, with the annualized exchange rate variation rate of 340 %, it is notorious that the price increase far exceeds the depreciation of the bolivar, which suggests that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is becoming dangerously overvalued in real terms," the observatory said.\par \par \uc2 Finally, it pointed out that this situation is causing sectors such as the agri-food and manufacturing industries to lag significantly behind commercial activities in terms of dynamism.\par \par \uc2 (With information from EFE)\par \par \uc2 CONTINUE READING:\par \par \uc2 Former foreign minister \uc2 Jorge Arreaza\uc2  registered as chavismo's candidate for the governorship of Barinas State\par \par \uc2 Barinas, time for the vote: Maduro's fraud in full view of the world\par \par \uc2 Venezuelan opposition leaders seek greater unity after \uc2 Julio Borges\uc2 ' announcement of interim government\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020211208ehc800475\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
