\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Venezuela's inflation was 8.1% in October, independent agency says\b0\par\par\uc2 300 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 November 2021\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 Caracas, Nov 8 (EFE) - Venezuela's monthly inflation was 8.1% last October, reported Monday the Venezuelan Observatory of Finance (OVF), an independent entity that brings together several economic analysts, who added that the year-on-year was 1,258% and the cumulative was 576.3%. The OVF maintained that the deceleration of inflation is due to the stability that the price of the dollar has maintained, due to the "recurrent \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 " made by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  (\uc2 BCV\uc2 ) "burning the international reserves to maintain without significant oscillations of the exchange rate". "The item that showed the greatest variation was recreation with 19.2%, followed by education with 11.8% due to the return to on-site classes, transportation with 11.3% and alcoholic beverages with 10.5%," he added.\par \par \uc2  As an effect of the monetary reconversion that came into effect in early October, with the elimination of six zeros to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the observatory indicated that there was also an increase in dollars in the prices of products and services. It also noted that the price of the food basket in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reached a historic high of $343.75 for a family of five, with a variation of 12.77% over the previous month, when it stood at $304.83."Thus, access to the food basket according to the minimum wage was 0.69%, while the minimum wage remained at 7 bolivars ($1.5)," he added. The observatory pointed out that these figures are estimated at the same time that it is declared the flexibilization of the measures by the pandemic of covid-19, the return to presential classes and the proximity of the regional and local elections of next November 21.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020211108ehb800ctr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
