\par\par \b \uc2 Venezuela to introduce 1-million-bolivar bill as inflation persists\b0\par\par\uc2 280 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2021\par 02:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright 2021 Thomson Reuters. All Rights Reserved. \par \par \uc2 CARACAS, March 5 (Reuters) - \uc2 Venezuela's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday that it would introduce a banknote worth 1 million bolivars beginning next week, as years of incessant hyperinflation continue to batter the value of the crisis-stricken South American country's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The new banknote will be worth just 52 U.S. cents at the current official exchange rate. Interannual inflation was running at 2,665% as of January, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The once-prosperous \uc2 OPEC\uc2  nation's economy has been in a tailspin for the past seven years, spurred by a collapse in oil prices that led to a drop in imports and a gaping fiscal deficit, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to print more bolivars.\par \par \uc2 "These new bills will complement and optimize the current denominations, to meet the requirements of the national economy," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said in a statement.\par \par \uc2 In addition to the 1-million-bolivar banknote, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it will introduce 200,000- and 500,000-bolivar banknotes to circulate alongside the 10,000-, 20,000-, and 50,000-bolivar bills currently in circulation.\par \par \uc2 Years of hyperinflation and erosion of the bolivar's value have led Venezuelans to use U.S. dollar banknotes for many everyday transactions. President Nicolas Maduro has called the informal dollarization process an "escape valve" while blaming U.S. sanctions for the economy's woes.\par \par \uc2 Critics say the root of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economic collapse lies in the \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies of Maduro and his socialist predecessor and mentor, \uc2 Hugo Chavez\uc2 . (Reporting by Deisy Buitrago Writing by Luc Cohen Editing by Leslie Adler) \par \par \uc2 Released: 2021-3-6T02:56:48.000Z \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020210306eh36002ut\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
