\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Fernandez said he "is wrong" the one who thinks he will "take distance from Cristina"\b0\par\par\uc2 1,020 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Oktober 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 We have something to offer youWith our digital subscription you will enjoy more than 300 exclusive items per month and ship our sites without limits. We have premium newsletters, an exclusive community for you, discounts with Club La Voz and more.\par \par \uc2 I want to subscribe from $30 President \uc2 Alberto Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez\uc2  assured that he "is wrong" who thinks that he will take "distance" from his vice president \uc2 Cristina Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez de Kirchner\uc2 , claimed the need to "be united" and assured that the Front of All should prevent "conservativeism from taking over Argentina again".\par \par \uc2 Fernandez thanked the governors for "the show of unity" for "getting ahead"In an interview that published the portal The Rocket to the Moon, Fernandez stated: "The act of October 17 (for Loyalty Day) is one of all of us; if someone's thinking of doing an act for me to take away from Cristina, they're wrong, because I'm not going to do it. What we need most is to be united."\par \par \uc2 It also recommended that anyone seeking to "strengthen the government" should do so by strengthening "everyone."\par \par \uc2 "I believe in collective projects. In this time it's my turn to be at the helm, but I'm part of this project. I'm gone once, twice I'm not leaving," he said.\par \par \uc2 He insisted that this is his "last project so that we all together do not allow conservativeism to take over Argentina again."\par \par \uc2 "If there's a partner in the CGT who thinks the solution is to throw another partner out the window, don't count on me, because we all need them here," he said.\par \par \uc2 Cafiero assured that a sector of the opposition "wants to harm" the governmentHowever, he admitted that he and Fernandez de Kirchner don't think "exactly the same about everything," but, he said, "Basicly and in the central engagement we have no fissure."\par \par \uc2 On Justice\par \par \uc2 In another order, consulted on the situation of the irregular transfers of judges Leopoldo Bruglia, Pablo Bertuzzi and Germ\u225\'00\'E1n Castelli, Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez considered that "obviously the Court (Supreme) should read that the lower courts are not thinking like them".\par \par \uc2 Regarding land-taking, he reiterated that it "does not endorse" these occupations, but raised that "criminal law does not fix a pressing social problem to be addressed, with the urbanization of fiscal land and the construction of housing for these people."\par \par \uc2 "The answer is not to shovel them with a judge and a policeman. It is a desperate act in the face of a society that is not giving answers," he mused.\par \par \uc2 Un\uc2  support for DD.HH. in Venezuela\par \par \uc2 With regard to Argentina's vote of support expressed days ago to the report of the United Nations High Commissioner for Human Rights, \uc2 Michelle Bachelet\uc2 , on the human rights situation in Venezuela, Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez noted that the country's position "did not change a shred" with respect to its original view of what is happening in the Caribbean country.\par \par \uc2 "For us, the work of the High Commissioner for Human Rights must continue and we must work together to ensure that the High Commissioner for Human Rights continues to work with the government of Venezuela and can set up an agency in Venezuela to work together. That was our vote, we didn't change an apex," he said.\par \par \uc2 "We repeated again that we are against meddling in Venezuela's domestic life, that we do not share the idea that \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  should endure any kind of military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , that we are against the blockade of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and that we must help the dialogue so that Venezuelans can find a way out. That was our vote. Here it was understood by a lightnessthat we had abandoned Venezuela and the truth is what we were doing is what we historically did," the President argued.\par \par \uc2 Last week, before the \uc2 Human Rights Council of the United Nations\uc2  (\uc2 UN\uc2 ), which took place in Geneva, Argentina, he also condemned the blockades and economic sanctions imposed on the country ruled by Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro, which "particularly assault the Venezuelan people".\par \par \uc2 The agreement with the \uc2 IMF\par \par \uc2 Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez stated that in Argentina it is necessary to "order the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market" for which, he considered, a program with the \uc2 International Monetary Fund\uc2  (\uc2 IMF\uc2 ) will be "fundamental".\par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market is very messy and we have to sort it out. In fact there are four different values," the representative said, noting that "the central problem is that because there are several dollar values, people end up confused and the media induces us to think more about the blue dollar."\par \par \uc2 The President stressed that between the August primary election and October 27 in which he won the election, "$23 billion leaked that they let out trying to hold a dollar that did not go past 60 pesos."\par \par \uc2 "When we arrived in December we found a languid, unreserved, empty \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  with few dollars of free availability. And we want to favor the use of those dollars in the purchase of import supplies, fundamentally," he explained.\par \par \uc2 In addition, he said that "there is a sustained demand from Argentines who want to save in dollars" which led to the implementation for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  treasure of the country tax and a 35% advance of the income tax.\par \par \uc2 "Liqui is a very small market, which moves no more than $20 million," he said, but also noted that "the blue dollar that is an illegal market, lacks dollars, because there is no tourism. Since there are fewer dollars, it tends to go up, it's a supply-demand game. It's not a big market either."\par \par \uc2 "By the end of the year we have to contain, because the pandemic is not over, it is at its worst right now. We lived it a little more relieved in the Amba. But inside it has been deployed with enormous ferocity."\par \par \uc2 POLICY SYNTHESIS Exclusive information and the best analysis, on Mondays in your mail. Enter your email Send Thank you for subscribing! An error has occurred, please try again later. Advertising\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020201011egab004fw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
