\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Tensions with US contribute to Turkey-Venezuela alliance\b0\par\par\uc2 727 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 2020\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 MEXICO CITY (AP) \u8212\'20\'14 At first glance they look like a strange couple.\par \par \uc2 But Turkey\u8212\'20\'14a power in the Mediterranean that is often irritated by what it calls Western \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionism\b0 \highlight\uc2 \u8212\'20\'14and \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2 , a Caribbean nation rich in oil and gold but in perpetual crises and under U.S. sanctions, have a few things in common.\par \par \uc2 There are economic ties; the most murky aspects have attracted scrutiny from the \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2 . They stand in solidarity in their anti-American discourse, even though the United States is one of Turkey's main trading partners. The personal relationship between the rulers of Venezuela and Turkey is warm, forged in part by words of mutual solidarity during internal attempts to expel them from power.\par \par \uc2 This alliance was evident Tuesday with Turkish Chancellor Mevlut Cavusoglu's visit to Caracas to sign agreements and commemorate the 70th anniversary of diplomatic relations between the two nations.\par \par \uc2 "There will be no sanctions, no blockades, no situation that prevents us from further deepening our integral relationship, and our economic and trade relationship in particular," Venezuelan Chancellor \uc2 Jorge Arreaza\uc2  said at a joint press conference with Cavusoglu.\par \par \uc2 The Turkish diplomat, who visited the Dominican Republic and Haiti before his arrival in Caracas, said his meetings in Venezuela focused on agriculture, construction, tourism, education and medical assistance. Despite the pandemic, the volume of trade between Turkey and Venezuela tripled in the first six months of this year compared to the same period in 2019, Cavusoglu noted without mentioning specific figures.\par \par \uc2 "We must continue," the Turkish minister declared. He told Arreaza that \uc2 Turkish Airlines\uc2  intends to become the first airline to resume flights to Caracas "when you open your airport".\par \par \uc2 The main international airport closed passenger flights due to the pandemic, although the number of airlines operating there had declined for years as the country fell into crisis. The economy deteriorated, political conflict and human rights abuses intensified, millions fled Venezuela, and U.S. sanctions virtually crippled its iconic oil industry, which has been struggling before.\par \par \uc2 Along with Russia and China, Turkey is among the small number of countries that represent a lifeline for Venezuelan President \uc2 Nicolas Maduro\uc2 , who has repelled the attempts of opposition leader \uc2 Juan Guaid\u243\'00\'F3\uc2  to depose him. The United States has made it increasingly difficult for these countries to do business with Venezuela, as happened last week when it confiscated the cargo of four ships allegedly transporting Iranian fuel to Venezuela. Iran said the United States had no right to confiscate shipments in international waters.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 U.S. Treasury Department\uc2  has also expressed concern about the gold venezuela says it flew to Turkey and the United Arab Emirates.\par \par \uc2 From early 2018, when \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves ran out, Venezuela began selling gold to pay for contracts, including some for a food distribution network that was used to carry out corruption in a plot allegedly led by Maduro's close friends, the department said.\par \par \uc2 A Turkey-based company run by Alex Saab, a Colombian entrepreneur linked to Maduro's circle, "bought goods in Turkey on behalf of Venezuelan customers, raising prices before selling them back to Venezuela," the department said last year.\par \par \uc2 Saab was arrested in Junecape Verde on his way to Iran and has challenged his extradition to the United States. Maduro's government said the businessman was traveling to Iran on a "humanitarian mission" to buy food and medical supplies.\par \par \uc2 Maduro, who seasons his speeches with socialist rhetoric, claims that American pressure amounts to an attempted coup. His personal relationship with Turkish President \uc2 Recep Tayyip Erdogan\uc2  began when he expressed solidarity after the Turkish ruler survived an assassination coup attempt by a group of military personnel in 2016. Erdogan returned the favor when Guaid\u243\'00\'F3, whose movement is currently inactive, was campaigning intensely against Maduro.\par \par \uc2 However, Turkey continues to operate within U.S. restrictions. Last year, Turkish bank Ziraat stopped working with \uc2 Venezuela's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  due to U.S. sanctions.\par \par \uc2 "Therefore, U.S. punitive measures that increase the cost of Turkey's relations with Venezuela could force Erdogan to reduce his support for Maduro," even if he continues to censor U.S. policy toward Venezuela, former Turkishiplomatic Imdat Oner wrote. In an analysis for the Washington-based Wilson Center, Oner described the relationship between Turkey and Venezuela as "an alliance of convenience."\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020200819eg8i00078\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
