\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 "Parallel" dollar steps on Bs. 32,000 and the official climbs to Bs. 27,900\b0\par\par\uc2 252 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 November 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The "parallel" dollar sits almost halfadays at around 32,000 bolivars, according to different portals that monitor its behavior, and keeps its homeless rise in sight. In contrast, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  offered at the BCV exchange tables seems to follow in its footsteps and this Wednesday its value is at Bs.27.962.02.\par \par \uc2 "Due to the new bullish rally of the parallel dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  activated its exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy with an estimated injection of 12 million euros in cash in the last 48 hours, in order to contain the seemingly unstoppable advance Of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the informal market," said the banking and business finance portal.\par \par \uc2 Recently, economist and director of eco-analytical firm Asdr\u250\'00\'FAbal Oliveros assured in a forum that the dollar could close on 45,000 bolivars in December, all with inflation that could hover around 5000%.\par \par \uc2 "The price of the dollar, at the end of this year could close about 45 thousand bolivars," Oliveros said.\par \par \uc2 In other statements, he added that "the dilemma for the Government is to contain the bolivars and not comply with the execution of the budget or spend everything and send the exchange rate above 90,000 Bs/$".\par \par \uc2 "In a study conducted between October 10 and 15 on 12,600 transactions, we recorded that 53.8% were in dollars," a recent analysis by ecoanalytics on his \uc2 Instagram\uc2  account said.\par \par \uc2 D