\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 The Chavista regime raised the minimum wage to 300,000 bolivars, equivalent to $15\b0\par\par\uc2 547 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Oktober 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 A wad of sovereign bolivars, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  that replaced the strong bolivar last year after inflation of 1,000,000% (Yuri CORTEZ / AFP)The Venezuelan regime of Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro announced on Monday a 375% increase in the minimum wage, which will now be 300,000 bolivars, according to the Chavista constituent Francisco Torrealba, in a measure that is far from covering the loss of capacity employees' purchasing.\par \par \uc2 "Happy Monday, new minimum income for all Workers in the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela has been established in 300 thousand Sovereign Bolivars of which 150 thousand correspond to Minimum Wage and 150 thousand to Cesta Ticket Socialista," explained Torrealba, who is also chairman of the Committee of Workers of the ultra-chavista National Constituent Assembly, whose functions are in conflict with the opposition National Assembly.\par \par \uc2 Torrealba accompanied its publication with an image of the Official Gazette announcing the increase.\par \par \uc2 This is the third recomposition of the minimum wage for the year, as Cocuyo Effect recalls, amid a brutal economic crisis with high levels of inflation, sharp falls in domestic gross product (53% between 2013 and 2018) and an uncontrolled increase in the dollar.\par \par \uc2 #FelizLunes New minimum income for all Workers in the Bolivarian Republic of Venezuela has been established in 300 thousand Sovereign Bolivars of which 150 thousand correspond to Minimum Wage and 150 thousand to Cesta Ticket Socialista. #ClaseObreraResteadaConMaduro pic.twitter.com/lwTe7l6mvT\par \par \uc2 \u8212\'20\'14 Francisco Torrealba (@torrealbaf) October 14, 2019In fact, at Monday's official exchange, the minimum wage is equivalent to $15.2 on the official market, and about $18 in parallel, according to the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Venezuela\uc2  cited by Cocuyo Effect.\par \par \uc2 According to National Assembly data, inflation for 2019 is at the moment at 3.336%, so the measure is hardly used to alleviate the situation.\par \par \uc2 Inflation reached 130,000% in 2018 according to official data, although other estimates speak of about 1,000,000%. The extreme situation led to a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange in August 2018, abandoning strong bolivars to adopt sovereign bolivars, a process that included removing several zeros.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Venezuela\uc2  (Reuters) (Marco Bello/)In January 2019 the minimum wage increased to 18,000 sovereign bolivars, and in April it did so to 40,000 (with 25,000 food basket), a derisory figure with which it was not even possible to buy a carton of eggs, but which remained until October.\par \par \uc2 Venezuela is also in the midst of an unprecedented political crisis, with a chavista regime that has been brutally repressed by opponents and is considered illegitimate by much of the international community, and an opposition national assembly elected in 2015 that appointed the legislator \uc2 Juan Guaid\u243\'00\'F3\uc2  as interim president, without being able to fully hold the office.\par \par \uc2 Against this backdrop, it is estimated that nearly four million people have left the country in recent years.\par \par \uc2 MORE ON THIS THEME:\par \par \uc2 An Army commander and former private secretary of Hugo Chavez increms the HighVenezuelan Military Command: "Bellacos, it is freedom that they had to defend!"Tough accusations, allegations of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and threats around the \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  case, during the presidential debate\par \par \uc2 Isolation and terror to betrayal: why Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro is almost no longer leaving Venezuela\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020191014efae005k8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
