\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Carlos Fern\u225\'00\'E1ndez-Vega: Mexico SA\b0\par\par\uc2 618 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Januar 2019\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 P Nobody is secret that, for six years, the Venezuelan economy is in crisis. Its dependence on oil income is practically total, and in that South American nation they came together broken up with disassembling: in 2013 \uc2 Hugo Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez\uc2  died, and that same year the collapse of the international prices of hydrocarbons began.\par \par \uc2 For those yesterdays the price of the Venezuelan oil basket was around 120 dollars per barrel, but from then on it sank, with the foreseeable economic consequences. Something similar happened in Mexico, although here the dependence on oil income was around 40 percent of the total. In the case of the South American nation, it approached 90 percent.\par \par \uc2 The decade prior to the collapse of oil prices, the Venezuelan economy recorded a 5.9 percent growth (\uc2 ECLAC\uc2  statistics) as an annual average, but as of that collapse, the situation worsened and since then it has been reporting negative numbers. In addition, Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro is not anywhere near Ch\u225\'00\'E1vez.\par \par \uc2 In this context, the United States has put the accelerator to the bottom and reinforces its coup attempt of 2002, always disguised as a crusade for democracy and pressing the community of nations to dress her brazen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , without forgetting, of course, that \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  has the largest oil reserves in the world.\par \par \uc2 How is the Venezuelan economy going? \uc2 ECLAC\uc2  offers us a thematic tour: in 2018 the gross domestic product (GDP) was reduced for the fifth consecutive year (15 percent), which represents an accumulated contraction of 44.3 percent compared to the 2013 record. On the other hand, since November 2017 presented monthly inflation rates higher than 50 percent, and in 2018 the monthly index averaged 128 percent.\par \par \uc2 Last year modifications were introduced to the exchange system and the official exchange rate of the bolivar against the dollar depreciated for the fifth consecutive year at rates that exceed 200 percent annually. In addition, international reserves registered a fall for the fourth consecutive year, and between December 2017 and November 2018, the decline was 9.1 percent.\par \par \uc2 Likewise, 2018 represented the fourth consecutive year in which oil production decreased, and the cumulative contraction between January 2013 and October 2018 exceeded 50 percent. This has caused that, in spite of the increase in prices of the Venezuelan oil basket, during 2017 and the first nine months of 2018 the Venezuelan public sector continues to depend on transfers of resources from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 The aforementioned increase in oil prices has allowed exports to grow 9 percent, which together with the decrease in imports (26 percent) produced a small surplus in the current account of the balance of payments, according to estimates of the Cepal.\par \par \uc2 In August 2018, the Venezuelan Executive Branch announced the Economic Recovery, Growth and Prosperity Program, consisting of a set of policy measures aimed at stabilizing inflation and resuming the path of economic growth.\par \par \uc2 By 2019, if the severe external constraint facing the country continues, a further fall in GDP (around 10 percent), rising inflation, a large increase in monetary aggregates and a significant depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  are expected.\par \par \uc2 As it is observed, the panorama is by other complicated, but instead of agreeing aid to surpass the economic crisis, the magical formula of Trump is the one of always: golpismo, with oil invoice.\par \par \uc2 The slices of the cake\par \par \uc2 By the way, the Russian news agency Sputnik released a balance sheet (Two centuries: from the invasion of Mexico onwards) to make clear what kind of democratization the United States has imposed on Latin America.Now that Venezuela is in the eye of the hurricane, it is worth remembering (see).\par \par \uc2 Twitter: @cafevega\par \par \uc2 cfvmexico_sa@hotmail.com\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020190128ef1s005vr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
