\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Latin America "builds" a legal wall against Venezuelan migration\b0\par\par\uc2 1,265 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 August 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN\uc2  points out that there are 2.3 million Venezuelans who left their country. A figure that can increase especially after the recent economic measures that gave Maduro (EFE) The massive migration of Venezuelans became the worst migration crisis in the history of Latin America; a drama that this week went around the world, but that has been overshadowed by the same affected region.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN\uc2  estimates that 2.3 million Venezuelans have fled their country. At this rate, they will be the largest number of displaced persons in the history of Latin America, and could even surpass those displaced by the Syrian crisis (6m). (Via @ TheEconomist)\par \par \uc2 Do we take it seriously? pic.twitter.com/yGtSqRFfcz\par \par \uc2 - Rodrigo Morales C (@Rodrigomoralesc) August 20, 2018\par \par \uc2 This Monday, August 20, the first pages of the mass media were dedicated to the great suffering that Venezuelans face today, not only in their country where Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro offered a series of announcements that formalize the devaluation of 95.8% of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  - figure according to the same \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Venezuela\uc2  -, but also the hardships to which they are subjected when leaving their land looking for a "better future".\par \par \uc2 From the New York Times, the Wall Street Journal, the big television platforms in England, France and Germany reflected the reality of a migratory crisis only comparable to that of Syria, while the rest of the media in Latin America, turned their eyes towards the new migratory measures that in the end, somehow, closes the doors to thousands of Venezuelans desperate to flee from a nation in ruins.\par \par \uc2 The crisis is such that the OAS convened an extraordinary meeting to deal with the mass migration of Venezuelans; While on Tuesday, the Government of Ecuador also convened a meeting to discuss the unusual migratory flows of Venezuelan citizens.\par \par \uc2 The Government of #Ecuador calls a meeting on September 17 and 18 in Quito to discuss the unusual migratory flows of Venezuelan citizens. Argentina, Brazil, Bolivia, Colombia, Costa Rica, Chile, Mexico, Peru, Paraguay, Panama, Dominican Republic, Uruguay and #Venezuela invited.\par \par \uc2 - Mariano de Alba (@marianodealba) August 21, 2018\par \par \uc2 And is that the governments of Colombia, Ecuador, Peru, Chile and Argentina made the decision to adjust their immigration laws to reduce the flow of Venezuelans for reasons of "security", although this announcement left thousands of Venezuelans on the verge of emotional collapse .\par \par \uc2 Despite the disparity of figures, the most recent and most stringent show that the emigration of citizens of this country, in the last two years, roughly equivalent to the population of cities such as Cartagena (Colombia), Arequipa (Peru) or a fourth part of the inhabitants of Caracas.\par \par \uc2 The \uc2 UN\uc2  points out that there are 2.3 million Venezuelans who left their country. A figure that can increase especially after the recent economic measures that gave Maduro in which he announced not only the devaluation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but also the increase in taxes and gasoline prices.\par \par \uc2 Between 2015 and 2017 the migration of Venezuelans to all parts of the world increased by 132%; in the case ofthose that go to countries of South America the increase was of 895%.\par \par \uc2 The "construction" of a legal wall began While the countries of the region have strongly criticized the president of the United States, Donald Trump for wanting to build a wall to prevent immigration, on the other hand the American continent begins to put obstacles against Venezuelans who flee desperate from their country. Measures that would also be causing many Venezuelan relatives can not meet under the principle of family reunification, a universal right.\par \par \uc2 Venezuelans without a passport are in the outskirts of the Ecuadorian city of Tulc\u225\'00\'E1n (EFE / Maria Paula Goyes) Colombia, Ecuador and Peru now demand that Venezuelans show their passports in order to enter; this, despite knowing the "impossible mission" that citizens face in order to acquire the document because the Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro regime paralyzed the delivery.\par \par \uc2 Getting a passport in Venezuela can cost about $ 1,000 on the black market, in a country where the salary does not exceed USD $ 2 per month.\par \par \uc2 The requirement of current passports was challenged by the Ombudsman of Ecuador, who requested precautionary measures before the courts to prevent the application of the measure. The Ombudsman, Gina Benavides, said that this requirement is not legal or constitutional, and ensures that it goes against "basic principles of humanitarian assistance."\par \par \uc2 The General Director of Migration Colombia, Christian Kr\u252\'00\'FCger Sarmiento, criticized Ecuador and Peru for demanding that those fleeing Venezuela present a valid passport.\par \par \uc2 "To demand passport today for Venezuelan citizens, when we know that their government is not issuing them, is to punish the people for the mistakes of their leaders, because we can not forget that Venezuelan citizens are leaving their country not for pleasure, but because of of the expulsion policy that Mr. Maduro has imposed, "said Kr\u252\'00\'FCger.\par \par \uc2 Venezuelan immigrants gather outside Tulc\u225\'00\'E1n in Ecuador (EFE / Maria Paula Goyes) To this measure of the passports, the announcement thatThe Peruvian government made the deadline for Venezuelans who enter the country before October 31 and can apply for the Temporary Permit of Permanence.\par \par \uc2 But Venezuelans who flee from the severe economic crisis, can not move through all the countries of the region with ease. Because countries like Chile or Panama also require a visa.\par \par \uc2 Last April, Chile announced the creation of the "democratic responsibility visa" for those Venezuelans who would like to work and remain temporarily in the country. A permit that can only be requested through the consulates of Chile in Venezuela.\par \par \uc2 For its part, in 2017, the government of Panama also began to demand a stamped visa for all Venezuelans who would like to visit that country for a maximum period of 30 days.\par \par \uc2 After Panama, Honduras, Nicaragua, Guatemala and El Salvador adhered to this regulation that requires a special visa for Venezuelans; while the 27 countries of the \uc2 European Union\uc2  require a passport with at least nine months of validity, round-trip tickets and, in some cases, even a letter of invitation and medical insurance. Venezuelans are fleeing their country with very little money in their pockets and with few belongings; Although they emigrate with the hope of achieving quality of life, they are becoming a great burden for the other nations of the region.\par \par \uc2 While that happens, many Venezuelans with dreams and illusions see how little by little they are "closing the doors" to emigrate, because we must remember that Nicol\u225\'00\'E1s Maduro has installed "kidnapping" as state policy, denying thousands of citizens the right to their passports; reason why the most expeditious solution was to leave the country by land and only with the identity card.\par \par \uc2 How to tell those migrants, who probably sold all their belongings, who can not reach their destinations and who have to return to a country in ruins? It is condemning thousands of Venezuelans to a state of depression without return. Above all, for those who are already in their destination country and who hope to reunite with their children and family.\par \par \uc2 Thus, while the whole world criticizes the wall that Trump plans to build between the United States and Mexico, Venezuelans are forced to face a humanitarian crisis unique in its contemporary history and also the "construction" of a legal wall to reduce its migratory flow The governments of the world refuse to be part of a military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but they also refuse to receive the thousands of Venezuelans who seek to save their lives and those of their relatives.\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180821ee8l005cf\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
