\par\par \b \uc2 Rubio Could Back 'Armed Forces' in Oil-Rich Venezuela -- Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,318 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2018\par 18:23\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 1222 ET - Florida Senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  signals possible support for military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \uc2 OPEC\uc2 -member \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2 , writing on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  this morning: "The world would support the Armed Forces in #Venezuela if they decide to protect the people & restore democracy by removing a dictator." Rubio's comments come as Secretary of State \uc2 Rex Tillerson\uc2  wraps up a trip to Latin American in which he said the US is more closely considering oil sanctions on Venezuela. Meantime, talks between Venezuela's government and the opposition aimed at solving an economic and political crisis collapsed this week, which led to President Maduro to set April 22 as his re-election vote, which many say would be rigged. (dan.molinski@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1214 ET - With EU Brexit negotiator \uc2 Michel Barnier\uc2  warning that a transition period immediately after Brexit in 2019 isn't a given, the prospect of businesses and households facing uncertainty ahead comes back into focus, says \uc2 Esther Maria Reichelt\uc2  , an analyst at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 . "The transitional deal was supposed to decrease the risk premium in sterling," Ms. Reichelt says, adding that "there is a huge uncertainty premium" in the pound at the moment. GBP/USD is down by 0.9% at 1.3786 after falling earlier to a more than three-week low of 1.3779. EUR/GBP is up by 0.7% at 0.8863. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 1012 ET - This week's equity sell-off is doing little to dispel expectations that the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  will continue with its rate rising cycle, analysts at BMI Research say. The global monetary policy trend has been toward increasing tightening, highlighted by an unexpectedly hawkish \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  announcement on Thursday, which suggested that not just one but two U.K. rate rises are on the table in 2018, BMI says. Real yields are also rising across the board, with the U.S. 10-year real yield hitting 0.76% on Friday, the highest since 2013. Higher real yields are a clear sign that the monetary tightening that is already underway is set to continue, BMI notes. (georgi.kantchev@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1006 ET - German rail operator \uc2 Deutsche Bahn AG\uc2  has placed an EUR750 million ($918 million) euro-bond with institutional investors from Europe, the company said. The bond has a tenure of 15.5 years and bears a coupon of 1.625%. The proceeds of the bond will be used to "increase \uc2 Deutsche Bahn\uc2 's financial flexibility," the company said in a statement. \uc2 Cr\u233\'00\'E9dit Agricole SA\uc2  , \uc2 Deutsche Bank AG\uc2  , \uc2 Mitsubishi UFJ Financial Group Inc\uc2  . and \uc2 UniCredit SpA\uc2  led the issuing consortium. (nina.trentmann@wsj.com ; @Nina_Trentmann)\par \par \uc2 0958 ET - Can the spreads of \uc2 Metsa Board\uc2  's 2.75% 2027 euro bond tighten further, given its strong performance since mid-December? \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  thinks so, expecting another 10-20 basis points of tightening if S&P upgrades the Finnish paper-and-pulp company to investment grade. S&P currently rates \uc2 Metsa\uc2  at BB+, the highest junk rating, with a positive outlook. And according to Danske , the company's credit metrics are now "comfortably past" S&P's threshold for an investment-grade rating. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com; @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0953 ET - The big decline in jobs registered in Canada's January employment report is unlikely to influence the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  's outlook, \uc2 TD Bank\uc2  economist James Marple says. He says the weak report is consistent with an economy moving to a more neutral rate of growth after a particularly strong 2017. "All told, this does not change the story for the Canadian economy much," Marple wrote. "The unemployment rate is still low with the economy remaining close to full employment." (kim.mackrael@wsj.com; @kimmackrael)\par \par \uc2 0936 ET - World growth prospects remain strong for 2018 and are unlikely to be derailed by recent financial market volatility, says \uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  . However, the balance of inflation risks is shifting, with implications for monetary policy, it says. "This has sparked a rise in global bond yields and significant equity market volatility," says \uc2 Brian Coulton\uc2  , \uc2 Fitch\uc2 's chief economist. "\uc2 Fitch Ratings\uc2  sees this primarily as a correction to an overly sanguine view on the U.S. interest-rate outlook rather than signaling any serious threat of a sharp economic slowdown," he says. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0926 ET - The already apparent scarcity of bunds--visible in lower liquidity and lower secondary market turnover--will continue not only until the end of the \uc2 European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  's asset purchases, say Daniel Lenz and \uc2 Sebastian Fellechner\uc2 , analysts at \uc2 DZ Bank\uc2  . As the \uc2 ECB\uc2  reinvests all maturing bonds, the shortage will remain or even increase until the \uc2 ECB\uc2  decides to reduce its balance sheet, they say. They explains this by saying that asset managers and insurers that have reduced their bund holdings due to low yield levels over recent years might return to the market and compete increasingly with the European System of Central Banks--the \uc2 ECB\uc2  and national central banks. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0906 ET - The eurozone's four largest issuers--Italy (up to EUR7.75 billion), Germany (EUR1.5 billion), France (up to EUR10 billion in nominal and inflation-linked bonds) and Spain (estimated EUR4.5 billion)--, plus Portugal (up to EUR1.25 billion) have scheduled government bond auctions for next week, aiming to sell up to around EUR25 billion in a test for investor appetite in the current market turmoil. Duration, however, "will be manageable," said Antoine Bouvet, rates strategist at \uc2 Mizuho\uc2 , as maturities stretch across the curve and five issuers. With supply significantly exceeding coupon payments, there will be positive net supply. (emese.bartha@wsj.com; @EmeseBartha)\par \par \uc2 0907 ET - Canada's latest jobs report suggests an earlier surge in employment creation may have been too good to be true, said Avery Shenfeld, chief economist at CIBC World Markets. Canada dropped 88,000 jobs in January, giving back roughly half of the significant gains that were registered late in 2017. "Market participants are getting schooled in the ways of Canada's employment numbers, and the lesson seems to be that when they're too good to be true, they might not be," Shenfeld wrote. (kim.mackrael@wsj.com; @kimmackrael)\par \par \uc2 0904 ET - \uc2 Victrex\uc2  has had a strong first quarter following favorable \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates and shipments for \uc2 Apple\uc2  's iPhones, \uc2 Liberum\uc2  says, and the investment bank lifts target price to 2,825 pence from 2,770 pence. A modest tailwind from the acquisition of aerospace and auto supplier \uc2 Zyex\uc2  also contributed to the U.K. polymer manufacturer's 41% revenue increase, \uc2 Liberum\uc2  says. Without these factors, the company's underlying performance has remained solid, with sales volumes rising about 10% to 11%, \uc2 Liberum\uc2  says. The investment bank upgrades its pretax profit forecast for the year ending Sept. 30 to GBP128 million, from GBP124.5 million. Shares are up 1.1% at 2,438 pence. (adria.calatayudvaello@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 0853 ET - Friday's close on the New York stock market will be key to determining if equity markets "can find support" or if they face "a more ominous downdraft," says \uc2 John Hardy\uc2  , \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at \uc2 Saxo Bank\uc2  . He warns the parallels with 1987--when U.S. market panic was mostly "a Friday-Monday one-two"--are "alarming." One source of worry is that the bond market is showing limited response to equity falls. "Most unsettling for so much money under management...is that 'risk parity' is not working at all at the moment as long yields have remained high [bonds very weak] even as we have outright carnage in equity markets," he says, also citing weak demand at \uc2 U.S. Treasury\uc2  auctions this week. (jessica.fleetham@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 09, 2018 12:23 ET (17:23 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180209ee29003oq\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
