\par\par \b \uc2 Global  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  and Fixed Income Roundup: Market Talk\b0\par\par\uc2 1,261 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Februar 2018\par 20:37\par \uc2 Dow Jones Institutional News\par \uc2 DJDN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2018, Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 The latest Market Talks covering \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  and Fixed Income. Published exclusively on Dow Jones Newswires throughout the day.\par \par \uc2 1437 ET - \uc2 Peru's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  left its reference interest rate unchanged on Thursday at 3%, but \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  says it could cut the rate by another 25bps in the coming months thanks to easing inflation. Also increasing expectations for another decrease is that economic growth will likely be weaker-than-expected, in part because of the unwinding of a fiscal stimulus and slower growth from China, Peru's biggest export market. "All this will cause Peru's export revenues to soften, in turn preventing a strong recovery in domestic demand," \uc2 Capital Economics\uc2  says. (ryan.dube@wsj.com; @duberyan)\par \par \uc2 1315 ET - Markets may be looking ugly, but according to these Fed growth trackers, the first quarter is still looking pretty sweet. The \uc2 Atlanta Fed\uc2  's GDPNow gauge is now at a 4% rise for the first quarter. The \uc2 New York Fed\uc2  's Nowcast is now a 3.3%. Both were updated today. (michael.derby@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1222 ET - Florida Senator \uc2 Marco Rubio\uc2  signals possible support for military \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \uc2 OPEC\uc2 -member \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2 , writing on \uc2 Twitter\uc2  this morning: "The world would support the Armed Forces in #Venezuela if they decide to protect the people & restore democracy by removing a dictator." Rubio's comments come as Secretary of State \uc2 Rex Tillerson\uc2  wraps up a trip to Latin American in which he said the US is more closely considering oil sanctions on Venezuela. Meantime, talks between Venezuela's government and the opposition aimed at solving an economic and political crisis collapsed this week, which led to President Maduro to set April 22 as his re-election vote, which many say would be rigged. (dan.molinski@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1214 ET - With EU Brexit negotiator \uc2 Michel Barnier\uc2  warning that a transition period immediately after Brexit in 2019 isn't a given, the prospect of businesses and households facing uncertainty ahead comes back into focus, says \uc2 Esther Maria Reichelt\uc2 , an analyst at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 . "The transitional deal was supposed to decrease the risk premium in sterling," Ms. Reichelt says, adding that "there is a huge uncertainty premium" in the pound at the moment. GBP/USD is down by 0.9% at 1.3786 after falling earlier to a more than three-week low of 1.3779. EUR/GBP is up by 0.7% at 0.8863. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 1212 ET - Slightly more than half of investors surveyed by the Nordic corporate bank SEB said they didn't have an opinion about the e-krona, a virtual \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 Sweden's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is thinking of creating to keep up with Swede reluctance to own physical money. Still, one third of respondents said "they have a positive attitude towards an e-krona and think its either a very good idea or at least think its should be investigated." In Sweden, demand for banknotes and coins is declining and the \uc2 Riksbank\uc2  is investigating whether an e-krona could be the solution to when the country stops using cash. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 1131 ET - The \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  is providing some stability for the sterling exchange rate, but it's unlikely the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will increase the interest rate by much during these times of uncertainty surrounding Brexit negotiations, says \uc2 Esther Maria Reichelt\uc2 , an analyst at \uc2 Commerzbank\uc2 . The fact that the \uc2 BOE\uc2  said on Thursday it was going to raise the policy rate earlier and faster than previously expected is just it being slightly less cautious and trying to catch up with the rest of the world, as global central banks move towards a tightening of their monetary policy, Reichelt says. (olga.cotaga@wsj.com; @OlgaCotaga)\par \par \uc2 1059 ET - The current strength of the euro against \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the Americas and Asia will have a significant impact on the earnings growth of Heineken in 2018, says Bryan Garnier. The broker estimates that the stronger euro will lead to a negative translation impact of EUR175 million on the brewer's adjusted earnings before interest and taxes for 2018 and beyond. Bryan Garnier says the Americas and Asia represented 28% and 26%, respectively, of Heineken's \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2016. The broker retains a buy rating on the stock. Heineken is due to report earnings for 2017 on Monday.(maryam.cockar@dowjones.com)\par \par \uc2 1013 ET - Mark Machin, CEO of Canada's largest pension fund CPPIB, says global stock and bond markets are entering a "very tricky" period as central bankers shift to tighten monetary policy after a period of unprecedented easing and "extraordinarily" low volatility. Compounding the uncertain monetary policy outlook, he says are recent and expected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  leadership changes in the United States, China, Europe and United Kingdom. "The market will have to get comfortable," with a new set of \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  chiefs, he says. Machin says the Canadian fund, which manages C$337.1B of assets, expects that interest rates will rise gradually as economic growth becomes more robust. (jacquie.mcnish@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1012 ET - This week's equity sell-off is doing little to dispel expectations that the \uc2 U.S. Federal Reserve\uc2  will continue with its rate rising cycle, analysts at BMI Research say. The global monetary policy trend has been toward increasing tightening, highlighted by an unexpectedly hawkish \uc2 Bank of England\uc2  announcement on Thursday, which suggested that not just one but two U.K. rate rises are on the table in 2018, BMI says. Real yields are also rising across the board, with the U.S. 10-year real yield hitting 0.76% on Friday, the highest since 2013. Higher real yields are a clear sign that the monetary tightening that is already underway is set to continue, BMI notes. (georgi.kantchev@wsj.com)\par \par \uc2 1006 ET - German rail operator \uc2 Deutsche Bahn AG\uc2  has placed an EUR750 million ($918 million) euro-bond with institutional investors from Europe, the company said. The bond has a tenure of 15.5 years and bears a coupon of 1.625%. The proceeds of the bond will be used to "increase \uc2 Deutsche Bahn\uc2 's financial flexibility," the company said in a statement. \uc2 Cr\u233\'00\'E9dit Agricole SA\uc2  , \uc2 Deutsche Bank AG\uc2  , \uc2 Mitsubishi UFJ Financial Group Inc\uc2  . and \uc2 UniCredit SpA\uc2  led the issuing consortium. (nina.trentmann@wsj.com ; @Nina_Trentmann)\par \par \uc2 0958 ET - Can the spreads of \uc2 Metsa Board\uc2  's 2.75% 2027 euro bond tighten further, given its strong performance since mid-December? \uc2 Danske Bank\uc2  thinks so, expecting another 10-20 basis points of tightening if S&P upgrades the Finnish paper-and-pulp company to investment grade. S&P currently rates \uc2 Metsa\uc2  at BB+, the highest junk rating, with a positive outlook. And according to Danske , the company's credit metrics are now "comfortably past" S&P's threshold for an investment-grade rating. (tasos.vossos@wsj.com; @tasosvos)\par \par \uc2 0953 ET - The big decline in jobs registered in Canada's January employment report is unlikely to influence the \uc2 Bank of Canada\uc2  's outlook, \uc2 TD Bank\uc2  economist James Marple says. He says the weak report is consistent with an economy moving to a more neutral rate of growth after a particularly strong 2017. "All told, this does not change the story for the Canadian economy much," Marple wrote. "The unemployment rate is still low with the economy remaining close to full employment." (kim.mackrael@wsj.com; @kimmackrael)\par \par \uc2 (END) Dow Jones Newswires\par \par \uc2 February 09, 2018 14:37 ET (19:37 GMT)\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJDN000020180209ee2900424\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw103\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal1545\pichgoal600
