\par\par \uc2 CE Noticias Financieras English\par \b \uc2 Omar Barboza: The petro is not constitutional\b0\par\par\uc2 518 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Januar 2018\par \uc2 CE NoticiasFinancieras\par \uc2 NFINCE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 Content Engine LLC \par \par \uc2 The president of the National Assembly Omar Barboza, indicated that the petro "is not constitutional", after having been approved the nullity of the cryptocurrency in the session that took place this Wednesday, January 10, the parliament.\par \par \uc2 "It is not constitutional, according to article 12, oil, natural resources, can not be given in guarantees ... Article 318 of the Constitution says that the monetary unit of Venezuela is the bolivar, and that only through international agreements , that \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are agreed between several countries, we ask to have a means of exchange different from the bolivar as a monetary unit, "he said in an interview with Venevisi\u243\'00\'F3n.\par \par \uc2 He also noted that "The hydrocarbons law in its third article prohibits giving oil as collateral," assuring that this economic measure is a form in which the government "evades its obligations."\par \par \uc2 "This is a way of evading the fulfillment of obligations again. If the government needs some solutions to the economic and debt issue, it simply has to do one thing so that it has our support ... if it is not approved by the National Assembly, it is null, "he added.\par \par \uc2 Concerning what in his opinion is a humanitarian crisis and the possible international \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he stated: "The Venezuelan people have to live at the cost of a parallel dollar that already goes above 140 thousand bolivars ... while those of the government have dollar to 10 (...) ".\par \par \uc2 In addition, he explained that money circulation "has to correspond to international reserves and national production" and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Venezuela\uc2  is "a banknote factory without backup."\par \par \uc2 "In 2014, in the month of April, the national monetary circulation was around one trillion bolivars, today it is over 12 trillion bolivars," he said on the subject.\par \par \uc2 After the approval of the national humanitarian alliance by the National Assembly, he explained that they will visit institutions to coordinate aid to the most needy: "We are going to visit many institutions, highly qualified and credible in the country, that can help tell all Venezuelans, let us put our hands in our hearts and we will help our compatriots who are suffering, who do not have how to satisfy their basic needs, and who help us, a bread flour, two kilos of rice, a clothing that it does not work for us. "\par \par \uc2 "We will ask the Episcopal Conference to assume this activity, in function that they can be recipients of the aids, so that they can fairly and transparently reach those in need," he said.\par \par \uc2 "We are going to go out and promote that alliance (...) It's not a political issue, it's a human issue," he stressed.\par \par \uc2 As for the legislative initiatives of the Assembly added: "We are of the criterion, that political change is a precondition to solve the underlying problems that Venezuelans are suffering ... that is why we are going to build, we are going to promote ... to rebuild the unity democratic as an alternative ... our call is that we can not give up fighting for Venezuela without trying to find a democratic alternative. "\par \par \uc2 Dokument NFINCE0020180111ee1b001xw\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
