\par\par \uc2 Top Stories\par \b \uc2 Venezuela to Use Diamonds to Boost International Reserves\b0\par\par\uc2 By Kejal Vyas \par \uc2 532 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Dezember 2014\par 13:04\par \uc2 Dow Jones Top Energy Stories\par \uc2 DJTES\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright \u169\'00\'A9 2014 Dow Jones & Company, Inc. \par \par \uc2 CARACAS--Venezuela, facing default fears amid an economic crisis and falling oil prices, will use diamonds as well as other precious stones and metals stored in its \b \highlight22\uc2 central-bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  vaults to boost international reserves, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said Thursday.\par \par \uc2 It will also incorporate easy-to-convert foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  into its reserves, the bank said in a statement explaining changes to a law regulating its activities. Venezuela's international reserves have dropped 28% in the last three years to $21.7 billion.\par \par \uc2 The country is likely to start holding some reserves in Chinese Yuan, a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official familiar with the matter said.\par \par \uc2 It is the latest effort by President Nicol&#225;s Maduro--whose approval rating hit a record low of 24.5%, according to a poll released this week--to try and salvage the oil-rich, but cash-poor economy. The country is facing crippling dollar shortages and scarcity of imported food and consumer goods. Its local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the bol&#237;var, is in free fall, reaching new lows almost daily.\par \par \uc2 But analysts said the new accounting methods for international reserves would do little to build trust among investors, who currently charge Venezuela one of the highest borrowing rates in the developing world.\par \par \uc2 "It looks like a cosmetic boost to the reserves which doesn't improve investor confidence and doesn't improve reserve liquidity," said Siobhan Morden, head of Latin America strategy at Jefferies in New York. "This is a strategy of counting pennies to see how long they have."\par \par \uc2 Venezuela holds more than 70% of its reserves in gold bullion. Having a small portion of the reserves in cash has been a concern for investors who worry about the country's ability to honor debt payments. Venezuela's benchmark 2027 sovereign bond offered a yield of more than 19% Thursday.\par \par \uc2 Mr. Maduro this week authorized a 20% cut in government spending in light of the more than 30% drop in the price of oil, which Venezuela relies on for 96% of its dollar income. Finance Minister Rodolfo Marco is in China this week seeking financing and will next head to allied countries like Russia and Iran, Mr. Maduro said.\par \par \uc2 Last month, Venezuela used a $4 billion loan from China, funds that are typically earmarked for infrastructure investments, to beef up its reserves. But reserves since have declined again by $1.8 billion.\par \par \uc2 "We have a special plan to strengthen our reserves," the president said in a speech Tuesday. "They're going to rise further in the upcoming weeks and beginning in January and February," he said, promising to open up the country's access to "freely convertible \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."\par \par \uc2 But those measures will only buy \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2  time without changes to its heavily \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2  economy and simplifying rigid \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls that maintain three different exchange rates for the dollar and deter investment, analysts said.\par \par \uc2 Barclays estimates that Venezuela's economy will be an outlier in the region this year, shrinking by 4.4%, followed by contractions of 6.2% and 1.5% in 2015 and 2016, respectively.\par \par \uc2 Write to Kejal Vyas at kejal.vyas@wsj.com\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJTES11020141205eac500007\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
