\par\par \b \uc2 Venezuela's Bolivar Weakens To VEF6.6 Against Dollar\b0\par\par\uc2 255 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 24 Februar 2010\par 17:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones News Service\par \uc2 DJ\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2010 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 CARACAS (Dow Jones)--The bolivar continued to weaken against the dollar in unregulated trading Wednesday, falling to its lowest level in two weeks as a dearth of dollars sold by the government continues to spawn demand in the parallel \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.\par \par \uc2 The bolivar traded at VEF6.6 against the dollar, weakening from the previous rate of VEF6.55. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has become a major player in \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2 's parallel \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market as it stopped selling its 90-day, zero-coupon dollar-denominated bonds.\par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  previously sold $260 million through the bonds, which serve as a backdoor tool for Venezuelans to get their hands on dollars and sidestep \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls. The issues haven't helped strengthen the bolivar and local news reports have indicated that Finance Minister Jorge Giordani is questioning the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bond sales as a device to prop up the bolivar.\par \par \uc2 Giordani said last Friday that the bond sales weren't geared at boosting the bolivar, a statement that seemed to contradict other government officials. President Hugo Chavez vowed in January to bring down the so-called black market rate to VEF4.3, the same level as the official rate.\par \par \uc2 Local daily El Mundo reported Tuesday that Giordani had halted the sale of a bond issued by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  that could top $750 million.\par \par \uc2 -By Darcy Crowe, Dow Jones Newswires; (58) 414 249 6821; darcy.crowe@dowjones.com [ 02-24-10 1142ET ]\par \par \uc2 Dokument DJ00000020100224e62o000ca\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw205\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal3075\pichgoal600
