\par\par \b \uc2 New Chavez Rival Blames Govt For Venezuela's Economic Woes   \b0\par\par\uc2 By Darcy Crowe   \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES   \par \uc2 849 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 11 Februar 2008\par 21:01\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2008 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.   \par \par \uc2 CARACAS (Dow Jones)--Venezuelan President Hugo Chavez's most formidable political opponent hasn't talked much about the country's economy, which is struggling with double-digit inflation and food shortages.   \par \par \uc2 But retired general Raul Baduel, Chavez's former armed forces commander, says one thing is clear: "A severe economic crisis is looming in \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and it has been brought about by state \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."   \par \par \uc2 Baduel, a close, long-time Chavez ally, defended the president during a brief coup in 2002, enabling Chavez's quick return to power. But in recent months Baduel has become a vocal critic, calling Chavez's failed bid in December to overhaul the Constitution through a referendum a coup of its own.   \par \par \uc2 The general blasted the proposed reform and caused a political storm as he became one of the most high-profile Chavez allies to turn around and condemn the administration. In a country devoid of popular opposition leaders, Baduel was transformed into a rallying figure for traditional Chavez detractors.   \par \par \uc2 His credentials also split the Chavez ranks and his denouncements were seen as a major force behind the referendum's defeat, Chavez's first electoral setback since he took office in early 1999.   \par \par \uc2 After the Dec. 2 vote, Baduel has kept his distance from the traditional political parties, and vowed to stay away from the races in regional elections slated for November. Instead, he has engaged in what seems like a quixotic bid to call for a constitutional assembly and fine-tune the current charter.   \par \par \uc2 Baduel admits he hasn't been able to garner much support, but says drafting the reforms let him "clear his head" on such thorny subjects as the Venezuelan economy.   \par \par \uc2 In a recent interview with Dow Jones Newswires, Baduel said after studying Venezuela's economic problems, he remains "a pragmatist."   \par \par \uc2 Most of his ideas, however, seem to be a direct indictment of Chavez's socialist-inspired economic policies, which he blames for "wasting the revenue of a historic oil bonanza."   \par \par \uc2 Propelled by high government spending, inflation, which has run rampant in recent years, "can only be fixed with traditional weapons like well-coordinated fiscal discipline and monetary policy," Baduel said.   \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has effectively become subordinate to the executive branch, with the result that real interest rates are now deeply negative.   \par \par \uc2 Baduel sees the erosion of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  independence as one of most grievous mistakes by the current administration. "The overwhelming evidence in the world shows that the greater the autonomy of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the lower the inflation figures," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Baduel, who said he has several economic advisers but was unwilling to disclose their names, noted that the officials in charge of monetary policy must be "shielded against populist demagoguery," and their professional advancement be uncoupled from national politics.   \par \par \uc2 The general also denounced what he called "the waste of billions" of dollars that have been funneled directly by the president to social programs that "have done little to change the plight of the poor."   \par \par \uc2 "If the government has the resources, it should spend them (wisely). But in Venezuela it's completely discretionary and depends on the president's whims," he said.   \par \par \uc2 Baduel's proposal - which is still being drafted - to reform the Constitution will include provisions to guarantee that social spending won't depend on the president, but will be regulated through pre-established mechanisms.   \par \par \uc2 Baduel said he still espouses the social equality ideals that brought him close to Chavez in their early days in the military, when together with two other young officers they pledged never to rest until they had "broken the chains of the powerful that oppress us."   \par \par \uc2 That oath, taken under a tree where 19th century South American Independence hero Simon Bolivar once rested, still stands, he says. "The state has a responsibility to the disenfranchised, but what we have seen lately is a rise in consumerism while the poor remain poor."   \par \par \uc2 His most scathing criticism was kept for \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  controls, which he blames for spawning a black market for dollars and causing distortions throughout the economy.   \par \par \uc2 Venezuela pegs the bolivar \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the dollar at a rate of VEB2.15, but the dollar often fetches double that amount in the parallel market. "Keeping those controls over a long period of time only creates economic problems," said Baduel.   \par \par \uc2 The general says he is not shy about running for office but argues that it's too soon to talk about a possible presidential bid. "I'm still sorting some ideas out in my mind," he said.   \par \par \uc2 -By Darcy Crowe, Dow Jones Newswires; (58) 212 564 1339; darcy.crowe@dowjones.com   \par \par \uc2 TALK BACK: We invite readers to send us comments on this or other financial news topics. Please email us at TalkbackAmericas@dowjones.com. Readers should include their full names, work or home addresses and telephone numbers for verification purposes. We reserve the right to edit and publish your comments along with your name; we reserve the right not to publish reader comments. [ 11-02-08 2001GMT ]   \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020080211e42b000vv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
