\par\par \b \uc2 Venezuelan Politics, Econ Controls Slam Economy In 2003  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Charles Roth  \par \uc2 Of DOW JONES NEWSWIRES  \par \uc2 906 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Februar 2004\par 23:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 NEW YORK (Dow Jones)--Political turmoil and heavy-handed state \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  took a huge toll on \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2 's economy in 2003.  \par \par \uc2 In a preliminary estimate, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported Tuesday the country's economy dove 9.2% last year, surpassing the previous year's 8.9% contraction.  \par \par \uc2 In dollar terms, gross domestic product withered to $83 billion in 2003 from $126 billion in 2001, said Alberto Ramos, Andean economist at Goldman Sachs in New York. "It's more than a recession; it's a collapse," he said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  placed a great deal of blame for the shrinkage in 2003 on a two-month nationwide general strike that brought the critical oil industry to a virtual halt. The strike was lifted last February, but year-old, government-imposed capital and price controls remain firmly in place. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also pegged to the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 After firing nearly half the workforce in the state-owned oil giant PdVSA in retaliation for going on strike, the Chavez administration was mostly successful in reestablishing oil production. For the year as a whole, though, oil production fell 10.7%.  \par \par \uc2 Despite improved administrative procedures in the second half for obtaining \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 , "the restrictions translated into transactional costs that affected the results of the principal macroeconomic variables," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  noted in its statement to the National Assembly.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  pointed out that it had approved a total of $14.3 billion from March through the end of December for \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  transactions, but a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange panel created to oversee domestic dollar sales only released $5.24 billion.  \par \par \uc2 "It's very clear part of the economic contraction was due to all the controls," Ramos said. While economically deleterious, politically they can be used to reward the administration's friends and punish its enemies, he added.  \par \par \uc2 The opposition staged the strike to force Chavez to resign or call early elections. They feared his self-proclaimed revolution is steering the country toward Cuban-style communism. Chavez denies it, and says his "oligarch" opponents just want their privileges restored.  \par \par \uc2 The opposition is now trying to advance a legal recall referendum on Chavez's mandate, though the outlook for the plebiscite remains unclear.  \par \par \uc2 The economic impact of the political uncertainty and the state \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  into the economy are also evident in the 8% shrinkage in non-oil output. The construction sector - significant for its multiplier effect - was the hardest hit, crumbling 37% last year.  \par \par \uc2 Balance of payments data also reflected the extent of the economic distortions. Thanks to the capital controls, international reserves ballooned $8.66 billion to $20.67 billion last year.  \par \par \uc2 Along with the economic freefall, the controls took a heavy toll on the trade account, badly affecting a country that imports more than 60% of all it consumes. Imports plunged more than 21%, while exports dropped 3.4%. The current account ended 2003 with a $9.62 billion surplus.  \par \par \uc2 The capital account, meanwhile, registered a $3.17 billion deficit, and the "errors and omissions" category showed a $1.01 billion outflow.  \par \par \uc2 Despite the price controls and economic depression, inflation still ran at 27% last year.  \par \par \uc2 Investment plummeted 39%, notwithstanding a marked fall in lending rates, a product of the increased liquidity wrought by the capital controls.  \par \par \uc2 The government tried to compensate for the drop in investment by jacking up spending, and sourcing a good portion of its funds from internal debt issuance.  \par \par \uc2 A 20% rise in domestic public debt - raising its total outstanding to 17.1% of GDP - likely spurred a recovery in the last months of the year, though that was also helped by a low base comparison. The sharp increase in liquidity was clear in the monetary base, which expanded more than 46% in 2003, making the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  dramatically increase its own monetary sterilization \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 But the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't yet released fourth quarter data, which \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director Domingo Maza Zavala's office told Dow Jones Newswires Wednesday was still being compiled and should be made public by the end of the month.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts are awaiting fourth quarter results and any revisions to data in previous quarters to draw firmer conclusions about current trends in Venezuela's economy.  \par \par \uc2 Some Wall Street houses expressed surprise by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's full year 9.2% contraction estimate, which would imply a major recovery in the fourth quarter after preliminary estimates of a 7.1% contraction in the third quarter, a 9.4% shrinkage in the second and a 27.7% nosedive in the first.  \par \par \uc2 In a Wednesday research note, Credit Suisse First Boston said it thinks "the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's estimate underestimates the economy's actual contraction." CSFB noted that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2 's full-year figures imply a 26.7% real increase in fourth quarter oil-sector GDP from the third quarter, compared with CSFB's own 4.0% estimated decline.  \par \par \uc2 On non-oil fourth-quarter GDP, CSFB expects a 0.8% rise from the third quarter, considerably less than the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's 5.9% advance.  \par \par \uc2 CSFB reckons Venezuela's economy dropped 11.9% last year from 2002, nearly three percentage points more than the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's own estimate.  \par \par \uc2 Ramos, the Goldman Sachs economist, estimated the country's GDP lost about 10% last year.  \par \par \uc2 -By Charles Roth, Dow Jones Newswires; 201 938 2226; charles.roth@dowjones.com  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020040218e02i000wy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
