\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela \highlight\uc2  Mkts: Bolivar Flat Although Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 417 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 September 2002\par 22:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  CARACAS -(Dow Jones)- The Venezuelan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  posted the bolivar's close at VEB1467.25 Monday, a bit weaker than Friday's VEB1467, despite efforts to boost the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The institution put in up to $25 million more than its preset daily $51 million buying bolivars, but steady demand for dollars prevented the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from strengthening, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  The institution reported that it bought bolivars at rates ranging from VEB1482.33 in the first of its three daily auctions to VEB1442 during the last. \par \par \uc2  Comments by President Hugo Chavez during the weekend increased dollar demand, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said. \par \par \uc2  Chavez said Venezuelans should "punish" private banks by transferring their money to state-run banks, because, he said, private banks are conspiring against the government by not buying public debt to help the government out of a cash crunch. \par \par \uc2  Bankers have said they can't risk exposure to Venezuela's deepening economic crisis, highlighted by a 7.1% contraction in the first half. \par \par \uc2  Analysts said Chavez's comments can't be taken seriously. \par \par \uc2  "People with money in the bank want Chavez out of office ... they aren't going to move money to government banks," said one local analyst who asked not to be quoted by name. \par \par \uc2  Indeed, Chavez's growing opposition - some 70% want him out of the presidency, according to local polls - have launched several separate efforts to oust him from office. \par \par \uc2  The president's primary support base consists of Venezuela's poor, most of whom reportedly have barely enough money to pay for their monthly needs, given annualized inflation of about 25%. \par \par \uc2  Local stocks ended mostly unchanged, with the IBC General Stock Index closed 86 points, or about 1.1%, higher at 7274 points. Of the IBC's 16 stocks, four gained, two closed lower, and 10 were unchanged. \par \par \uc2  Just 1.9 million shares valued at VEB293 million changed hands, compared with 1.3 million shares valued at VEB151 million Friday. \par \par \uc2  Telephone giant CA Nacional Telefonos de Venezuela lost VEB25.00 to end at VEB2350.00 while its American Depositary Receipts, worth seven common shares apiece, ended at $11.36, down 41 cents on the New York Stock Exchange. \par \par \uc2  There were no public debt auctions Monday. \par \par \uc2  On the Web: \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 : {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bcv.org.ve/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bcv.org.ve}}}\par \par \uc2  Caracas Stock Exchange: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.caracasstock.com/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.caracasstock.com}}}\par \par \uc2  -By Jehan Senaratna, Dow Jones Newswires; 58 212 564 1339; jehan.senaratna@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1155 1864 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020916dy9g00151\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
