\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela \highlight\uc2  Bolivar Ends Up; Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 293 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 August 2002\par 21:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  CARACAS -(Dow Jones)- The Venezuelan \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported the bolivar's official close Wednesday at VEB1373.88 per dollar, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  took advantage of a slow session to bolster the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  Wednesday's close was stronger than VEB1383.38 Tuesday because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  with about $10 million more than its standard daily $45 million, buying the bolivar at rates ranging from VEB1388.57 down to VEB1361.92. \par \par \uc2  Trading was slow because most investors have adopted a "wait and see attitude" about a critical Supreme Court ruling expected to be announced later in the day, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  But dollar demand is still generally high given increased political uncertainty which has already resulted in street gun battles and general violence, the dealer said. \par \par \uc2  The Supreme Court is expected to announce whether four military commanders will be charged in connection with  President Hugo Chavez's brief ouster in April. \par \par \uc2  Analysts have said a decision to not charge the officers will likely be seen as positive for markets because it would be detrimental to the left-leaning Chavez's presidency. \par \par \uc2  However, the bolivar is expected to continue devaluing beyond VEB1500 against the dollar by the end of this year because it would help the government meet its obligations. \par \par \uc2  Given that more than half the government's income is in dollars, a weaker bolivar will give officials more money in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cover this year's financing needs equal to about 9% of the country's $100 billion gross domestic product. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Website: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bcv.org.ve"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.bcv.org.ve}}}\par \par \uc2  -By Jehan Senaratna, Dow Jones Newswires; 58 212 564 1339; jehan.senaratna@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1155 1864 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020020814dy8e0018j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
