\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela \highlight\uc2  Bolivar Weakens To VEB760; Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 207 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2002\par 18:56\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2002, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  CARACAS -(Dow Jones)- The Venezuelan bolivar closed weaker against the dollar Thursday after strong \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to balance high dollar demand, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The bolivar ended at VEB760 to the dollar, VEB1 weaker than Wednesday's official VEB759 close. \par \par \uc2  Demand for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was high, and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fulfilled about $130 million out of a total $250 million traded, a trader at a local bank estimated. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which by law must buy most of the dollars earned by state-owned oil monopoly Petroleos de Venezuela SA, is the biggest supplier of dollars to the market. \par \par \uc2  Liquidity eased further and the overnight rate ended at an average of 6% on volume of about VEB100 billion, according to dealers. \par \par \uc2  A government official again dismissed speculation about capital controls if the bolivar slipped too far off the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's intended 10% depreciation this year. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director Domingo Maza was quoted in local media as saying the government would maintain higher interest rates as an alternative to dollar purchases. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Web site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bcv.org.be"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.bcv.org.be}}}\par \par \uc2  -By Jehan Senaratna, Dow Jones Newswires; 58 212 564 1339; jehan.senaratna@dowjone