\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela \highlight\uc2  Bolivar Ends At VEB757.50 As Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 296 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 Dezember 2001\par 18:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  CARACAS -(Dow Jones)- The Venezuelan bolivar ended considerably stronger against the dollar Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  acted to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The bolivar ended VEB9.00 stronger at VEB757.50 to the dollar, just VEB7.50 weaker than the government's year-end target. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  stepped in after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was quoted at around VEB780.00 earlier in the session, a trader at a local bank said. \par \par \uc2  "Trading was lighter than usual because of the New Year's Eve holiday," the trader said. \par \par \uc2  "But dollar demand will likely pick up in the first week of next year and the bolivar will probably drop again," he added. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has struggled over the last two weeks to keep the bolivar to its programmed trading band whose central parity was supposed to end the year at VEBB750.00. \par \par \uc2  Just Friday, market sources said the institution used up about $300 million out of a total $600 million in trades, but failed to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from dropping to VEB766.50. \par \par \uc2  Monday, given the lower volume and slack dollar demand, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  only sold about $100 million out of about $200 million traded, according to dealers. \par \par \uc2  The institution, which by law must buy most of the dollars earned by state-owned oil monopoly Petroleos de Venezuela SA, is the biggest supplier of dollars to the market. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate averaged about 37% on about VEB80 billion in volume. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said it plans to devalue the bolivar 10% in 2002, starting at Monday's close. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Web site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bcv.org.be"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.bcv.org.be}}}\par \par \uc2  -By Jehan Senaratna, Dow Jones Newswires; 58 212 564 1339; jehan.senaratna@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1155 1864 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011231dxcv000sj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
