\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela \highlight\uc2 's Bolivar Closes Stronger As Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 217 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2001\par 19:44\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  CARACAS -(Dow Jones)- The Venezuelan bolivar closed stronger against the dollar Thursday with \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  forcing holders of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to unwind their positions, according to dealers. \par \par \uc2  The bolivar ended at a midrate of VEB698.25 to the dollar, VEB0.50 stronger than Wednesday's VEB698.75 close. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action forced other banks to unload their dollars, strengthening the bolivar, said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer at a local bank. \par \par \uc2  "Every January, in the first few weeks of the year, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to get long dollar positions unwound and that's what it did today," he said. \par \par \uc2  Traders estimated the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold around $40 million dollars. Total market volume was estimated at $90 million. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  by law must buy most of the dollars earned by state-owned oil monopoly Petroleos de Venezuela SA and is the biggest supplier of dollars to the market. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate ended with an average of around 5% on about VEB100 billion in volume, according to dealers' estimates. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, the overnight rate traded between 4% and 33%, averaging 17.8% on market volume of about VEB150 billion. \par \par \uc2  -By Jehan Senaratna, Dow Jones Newswires; 582-564-1339; jehan.senaratna@dowjones.com \par \