\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela \highlight\uc2  Bolivar Gains Vs Dlr After Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 203 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2000\par 20:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2000, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  CARACAS -(Dow Jones)- The Venezuelan bolivar (VEB) gained against the dollar Thursday as the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  just before the session ended, countering investors who were seeking a safe haven in the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of Sunday's general elections, dealers said. \par \par \uc2  The bolivar ended at a midrate of VEB687 per dollar, stronger from Wednesday's close of VEB687.50 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "There was a strong dollar demand across the board from banks to private customers due to the upcoming elections," a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader at a local bank said. "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  15 minutes before the session closed, only to show the market they're capable and willing to defend the bolivar," the trader added. \par \par \uc2  Total dollars traded, including transactions between banks, was about $110 million, of which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  accounted for some $70 million, he estimated. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is usually the biggest supplier of dollars to the market and it tightly controls the bolivar's exchange value. \par \par \uc2  The overnight rate remained stable at 4%, unchanged from Tuesday's market close, the trader said. \par \par \uc2  -By Fred Pals, Dow Jones Newswires; 582-564-1339; fred.pals@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1155 1864 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010805dw7r03ns6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\p