\par\par \b \uc2  Caracas shares lose 0.28 pct, bolivar weaker. \b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 November 1999\par 22:25\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CARACAS, Nov 23 (Reuters) - Caracas stocks slipped for a second day Tuesday, losing 0.28 percent, as investors continued to avoid the market ahead of a December 15 referendum on a controversial new constitution. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The bolivar \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 \tab   also weakened as the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Central Bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  trimmed its sales of dollars despite steady demand from local businesses.\par The IBC index\tab   of leading shares lost 15.14 points to close at 5,464.24 points, with 14 stocks stable, five rising and five falling.\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  "I don't think there will be much interest in investing in the local market until the new constitution is approved," said Miguel Ortiz of the Patagon.com brokerage. \par \par \uc2  While populist President Hugo Chavez has staked his political future on the approval of the new charter, it has elicited strong criticism from business leaders and opposition politicians who say it is economically backward and \b \highlight22\uc2 interventionist\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  National telephone company CANTV  , \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2 's largest publicly traded company, lost 1.44 percent to close at 2,400 bolivars a share. Benchmark share Electricidad de Caracas  gained 0.93 percent to end at 223.05 bolivars each. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the national \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed 0.5 bolivar weaker at 635.75/636.75. \par \par \uc2  Traders said demand for the dollar was boosted because foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought Tuesday is payable one day later than usual due to Thursday's Thanksgiving national holiday in the United States. \par \par \uc2  The exchange rate will remain fixed Thursday at the previous day's close. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Director Armando Leon said Tuesday the bank had sold around 20 to 30 percent less foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  this year than in 1998 due to the deep recession gripping Venezuela. \par \par \uc2  ((Ana Isabel Martinez, Caracas newsroom 582 505 2600, fax 582 861 3621, caracas.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010908dvbn09it8\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
