\par\par \b \uc2  Venezuelan Bolivar Closes Weaker At VEB582.00/Dlr \b0\par\par\uc2 273 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 31 August 1998\par 20:43\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  CARACAS (Dow Jones)--The bolivar closed weaker Monday against the dollar in active trading as excess liquidity in the financial system pushed banks into dollars, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The bolivar closed at a midrate of 582.00 bolivars per dollar, down from Friday's close of 581.00. \par \par \uc2  The average bank spread was 581.50/582.50 bolivars. Spreads for major banks ranged from 581.50/582.50 to 582.00/583.25. \par \par \uc2  After being interrupted by a credit crunch in the past two weeks, commercial banks resumed their dollar-buying activities on Monday as the financial system remained awash in cash. \par \par \uc2  The lending rate in overnight, interbank market - a key indicator of liquidity - was at 8% at midday Monday, up from Friday's close of 5%, but still sharply lower than Thursday's close of 90%. \par \par \uc2  Once dollar-buying pressure sent the bolivar to around 582.50 bolivars per dollar by early afternoon, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  by heavily selling the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , causing the dollar to yield some of its earlier gains, traders said. \par \par \uc2  After standing mostly to the sidelines in the morning, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold roughly $60 million to $80 million during the entire day, according to traders' estimates. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2 , which by law must buy most of the dollars earned by\par state-owned oil monopoly Petroleos de Venezuela SA (PDVSA), is the\par biggest supplier of dollars to the market. It sells roughly $30 million\par to the market on a typical day.\par    -By Greg Cancelada; 582-564-3291\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 31-08-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1843GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1155 1864 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du8v07h57\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
