\par\par \b \uc2  Venezuela bolivar ends softer in quiet trade. \b0\par\par\uc2 204 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 August 1998\par 21:28\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CARACAS, Aug 18 (Reuters) - The Venezuelan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the bolivar, closed softer in quiet trade after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  met most of a small increase in corporate hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  demand with dollar sales, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The unit closed at 571.75/572.75 per dollar, versus Monday's close of 571.00/572.00 per dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The market remains calm, although I've seen a small increase in corporate demand," one trader said. But "the demand was normal, just to meet imports and hard \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs," he added, noting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dollar sales into the market. \par \par \uc2  As the sole recipient of state oil company PDVSA's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is by far the largest actor on \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, blurring the difference \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and meeting real demand. \par \par \uc2  Traders added they expected interest rates to edge ahead at Wednesday's auction of Monetary Stabilisation, or TEM, bills, further adding to the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market's recent calm. \par \par \uc2  Last week, yields on 27-day TEMs rose 21 basis points to 46.89 percent. \par \par \uc2  ((-Yelitza Cova, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600, fax 582 861 3621, caracas.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021216du8i01111\par }\pa