\par\par \b \uc2  Venezuela bolivar slide slows on cenbank dlr sales. \b0\par\par\uc2 330 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 August 1998\par 22:16\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  CARACAS, Aug 13 (Reuters) - Venezuela's bolivar \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened Thursday, but at a much gentler rate than in recent days due to heavy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sales by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The bolivar closed at 570.00/571.00 per dollar from 569.75/570.75 per dollar on Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The bolivar has depreciated by 1.3 percent in the last week and traders said pressure on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  continued Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "The demand (for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is being fuelled by the expectation that the exchange rate will continue to rise as it has done in the last three days," one trader said. \par \par \uc2  As the sole recipient of state oil company Petroleos de Venezuela's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  earnings, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is by far the largest actor on \b \highlight22\uc2 Venezuela\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets, blurring the distinction between \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and meeting real demand. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was participating throughout the day, offering a good amount of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," another trader said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Antonio Casas Gonzalez said in an interview with local Union Radio Thursday that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was seeking to encourage exchange rate stability. \par \par \uc2  "Obviously when demand (for foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) is too high the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is limited as to how much it can participate and that is what has happened on some days recently when the exchange rate has risen more than in other situations," Casas said. \par \par \uc2  The exchange rate remains well within the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's ample \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band which has upper and lower limits 7.5 percent either side of a sliding central rate. \par \par \uc2  But traders note that while the exchange rate followed the central rate fairly closely for the first half of the year, since June it has diverged. \par \par \uc2  According to calculations by Reuters the central rate is about 556 bolivars per dollar at the moment. \par \par \uc2  ((-Yelitza Cova, Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600, fax 582 861 3621, caracas.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020021113du8d032ct\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
